    ["raster_image_files",
    ".FPX",
    "FlashPix Bitmap Image File",
    "3.6",
    "Picture saved in the Kodak FlashPix format, a bitmap image format optimized for digital photography; used by the Picture Easy Software application included with Kodak digital cameras. The FlashPix format was developed by Kodak, along with partners Microsoft, Hewlett-Packard, and Live Picture. Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Microsoft Picture It! —  (Discontinued). IrfanView. XnViewMP. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Microsoft Picture It! —  (Discontinued). IrfanView. XnViewMP. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".VPE",
    "Photoshop Vanishing Point Export File",
    "3.6",
    "File created by the Extended version of Adobe Photoshop, a professional graphics editing application; saves vanishing point planes that have been specified by a designer on a 2D image; can be imported into After Effects, which splices the 2D image into different images represented by the planes. Vanishing points are used for specifying the 3D geometry of a 2D image, such as placing planes on a picture where youre looking through a tunnel or at a road off into the horizon. After importing into After Effects, you can add lighting or other effects that make the original 2D image look three-dimensional. To import a VPE file into After Effects, choose File → Import → Vanishing Point (.vpe).. To create a VPE file in Photoshop Extended, choose Filter → Vanishing Point.., draw the shape of your planes, and then select Export for After Effects from the Vanishing Point window. Windows Adobe After Effects 2023. Mac Adobe After Effects 2023.",
    "Windows Adobe After Effects 2023. Mac Adobe After Effects 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".FBM",
    "Fuzzy Bitmap Image",
    "3.6",
    "Graphic file format saved by FBM (Fuzzy Pixmap Manipulation), an application toolkit used to manipulate and convert images; rarely used anymore, but still may be viewed using XnView, as well as a few other programs. Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Linux xli. An FBM file contains a model created by DELFTship or FREE!ship, which are programs used to create 3D designs of marine vessels. It stores information about the model, such as the length, width, and volume. FBM files also include metadata, including the model description, creator, and date created. You can open FBM files in DELFTship by selecting File → Import. You can open FBM files in FREE!ship by selecting File → Open. NOTE: The DELFTship name comes from Delft University of Technology, which is where the software was originally developed. Windows DELFTship. FREE!shipFree.",
    "Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Linux xli. Windows DELFTship. FREE!ship.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".FIL",
    "Symbian Application Logo File",
    "3.6",
    "A FIL file is a database table created by ACL for Windows. It contains a data set used in an ACL project. FIL files are flat files that contain raw data, and they must be linked to an ACL table layout to be used in ACL for Windows. ACL for Windows, which has previously been known as ACL Analytics and ACL Desktop, is a data analysis and reporting application. It allows users to, among other things, identify trends and exceptions among data, track compliance with organizational or governmental standards, and perform automated analytic testing. Data analysts using ACL create one or more projects to import, analyze, and report on data. These project files contain many constituent files, including FIL files. Each FIL file contains the data associated with a specific database table. FIL files do not, however, contain table layout information, which ACL uses to show data to users. Therefore, you must either import an associated table layout file before you import a FIL file into ACL, or you must create a new table layout as you import your FIL file. You can import a FIL file into ACL for Windows to view the data it contains. Note that you must also import or create an associated table layout to view the data your FIL file contains. If your FIL file is stored within an ACL project you have access to, it may be easier to import the FIL files data using the Copy from another Project → Table.. option available in ACL. To access this option, right-click your current projects name in the ACL navigation bar. Windows ACL for Windows. Contains bitmap (.BMP) images used for the Nokia logo and Symbian S60 smartphone application icons; typically includes multiple resolutions of the logo; can be viewed using the Symbian Image Viewer program, which is included with the S60 software. Windows Transfer to a Symbian-based phone Mac Transfer to a Symbian-based phone.",
    "Windows ACL for Windows. Windows Transfer to a Symbian-based phone. Mac Transfer to a Symbian-based phone.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PGM",
    "Portable Gray Map Image",
    "3.6",
    "A PGM file is a grayscale image file saved in the portable gray map (PGM) format and encoded with one or two bytes (8 or 16 bits) per pixel. It contains header information and a grid of numbers representing different shades of gray, from black (0) to white (up to 65,536). PGM files are typically stored in ASCII text format but also have a binary representation. PGM file open in Apple Preview 11 PGM files include a header that defines the PGM format type (P2 for text or P5 for binary), image width and height, and the maximum number of shades. While binary PGM files may contain multiple images, ASCII PGM files may only include one image. The PGM format is one of several image formats defined by the Netpbm project, which is an open-source package of graphics programs. Other formats include the portable bitmap (.PBM) and portable pixmap (.PPM) formats. NOTE: PGM files may also be called portable greymap files. You can open a PGM file with various image viewers and editors. Some applications that support PGM images include GIMP (multiplatform), Corel PaintShop Pro (Windows), and Apple Preview (bundled with macOS). Opening a PGM file with a text editor PGM file open in Apple TextEdit Since PGM files are saved in plain text, you can also open them with a text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad or Apple TextEdit, or a source code editor. You may need to rename the.pgm file extension to.txt for the text editor to recognize it. When opened in a text editor or source code editor, you can modify the image data in a PGM file. However, if you incorrectly edit the file, you may inadvertently corrupt the image. Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. GIMP. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Inkscape. Netpbm. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plug-in. Any text editor Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. Inkscape. Netpbm. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plug-in. Any text editor Linux GIMP. Inkscape. Netpbm. Any text editor Android File Viewer for Android. A PGM file contains a program used by various Music Production Controller (MPC) devices, such as MPC1000, MPC2000, and MPC3000. It stores configuration information about the pads (buttons) on the MPC device and the mono or stereo samples they are assigned to play when touched on the MPC device. PGM files also include parameters for the program, such as sound assignments, SIMULT settings, and tuning parameters. PGM files may be saved in the standard MPC program format or the revised format that was developed to support more complex MPC devices. MPCs manufactured before the MPC1000 device do not support the newer PGM format. However, MPCs manufactured after the MPC1000 support both versions of the PGM format. While PGM files were designed to be loaded on to MPC devices, they can also be loaded by MPC software developed to emulate MPC devices on computers. Some examples of programs that can open PGM files are MPC Maid and MPC Editor. Windows MPC Maid. Midicase.com MPC Editor. Native Instruments Maschine 2. Mac MPC Maid. Native Instruments Maschine 2. SS Works RS-16X.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. GIMP. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Inkscape. Netpbm. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plug-in. Any text editor. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. Inkscape. Netpbm. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plug-in. Any text editor. Linux GIMP. Inkscape. Netpbm. Any text editor. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows MPC Maid. Midicase.com MPC Editor. Native Instruments Maschine 2. Mac MPC Maid. Native Instruments Maschine 2. SS Works RS-16X.",
    "Several image editors, including GIMP, Corel PaintShop Pro, and Apple Preview, can convert PGM files to other formats. For example, GIMP can convert PGM files to many file types, including the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.BMP - Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PS - PostScript File.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.WEBP - WebP Image.EXR - OpenEXR Image.XCF - GIMP Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".IWI",
    "Infinity Ward Texture File",
    "3.6",
    "Graphics file used by the Infinity Ward game engine, which was used for some Call of Duty and James Bond first-person shooter games; stores textures for game models; used for overlaying graphics on NPCs, weapons, buildings, terrain, and other objects. IWI textures can be converted to the.DDS format using IWI_X_DDS. NOTE: The Infinity Ward engine was developed using the id Tech 3 Doom 3 Engine as a baseline. It adds several lighting effect enhancements. Windows Activision Call of Duty: Black Ops. Activision Call of Duty: World at War. Activision Call of Duty 4: Modern Warfare. Activision Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2.",
    "Windows Activision Call of Duty: Black Ops. Activision Call of Duty: World at War. Activision Call of Duty 4: Modern Warfare. Activision Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".MDP",
    "FireAlpaca Image",
    "3.6",
    "An MDP file is an image created by MediBang Paint Pro, a free painting and comic creation application for Windows, macOS, Android, and iOS. It is the native format used to save images in MediBang Paint Pro. MDP files store one or more layers, which may include annotations, stencils, masks, and other shapes. MDP file open in MediBang Paint Pro 21 The MDP file is the primary file type associated with MediBang Paint Pro. The format is only supported by MediBang Paint Pro, but can be exported to more popular formats, such as.PNG,.JPG,.BMP,.TIFF,.WEBP, and.PSD. You can create an MDP file in MediBang Paint Pro by selecting File → New.. then selecting File → Save or Save As.. and selecting the MediBang Paint Pro format. You can open an MDP file in MediBang Paint Pro by selecting File → Open.. and choosing the MDP file. Windows MediBang Paint Pro. Mac MediBang Paint Pro. iOS MediBang Paint for iOS. Android MediBang Paint. Settings file created by Visual C++ 5, a program used to develop Windows programs using the C++ programming language; stores the workspace configuration settings; used for saving and loading customized workspace layouts. NOTE: Visual C++ is included with Microsofts Visual Studio software development tool. Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. An MDP file is an image file created by FireAlpaca, a free paint tool for Windows and macOS. It is the native format used to save images in FireAlpaca, which may include multiple image layers, masks, stencils, annotations, filters, and other elements. MDP file open in FireAlpaca 2 The MDP file is the primary file type associated with FireAlpaca. It is used to save images that can be closed and reopened by FireAlpaca for further editing. However, the format is not widely supported. Therefore, when you are finished editing your image in the MDP file you can export the file as a.PNG,.JPG,.BMP, or.PSD file. You can create an MDP file in FireAlpaca by selecting File → New.. then selecting File → Save or Save As.. and selecting the FireAlpaca format. You can open an MDP file in FireAlpaca by selecting File → Open.. and choosing the MDP file. Windows FireAlpaca. Mac FireAlpacaFree.",
    "Windows MediBang Paint Pro. Mac MediBang Paint Pro. iOS MediBang Paint for iOS. Android MediBang Paint. Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Windows FireAlpaca. Mac FireAlpaca.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".JPE",
    "JPEG Image",
    "3.6",
    "24-bit compressed JPEG graphic format that is commonly used for Web graphics; best suited for photos or images that contain lots of colors; also used by most digital cameras for saving digital photos. JPEG images use lossy compression, which means some image quality is lost when the compression is applied. The more compression is used, the less clear the image will appear. NOTE: JPEG files most often use the.JPG extension. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Illustrator 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Axel Rietschin FastPictureViewer. Any image viewer Any web browser Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Any image viewer Any web browser.",
    "Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Illustrator 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Axel Rietschin FastPictureViewer. Any image viewer Any web browser. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Any image viewer Any web browser.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PSB",
    "Photoshop Large Document Format",
    "3.6",
    "A PSB file is an image file created by Adobe Photoshop, a professional image-editing application. It contains an image that is larger than 30,000 x 30,000 pixels or 2 GB in size. PSB files are nearly identical to.PSD files except that they contain large images, so they tend to have large file sizes. PSB file open in Adobe Photoshop 2022 When a Photoshop user wants to save an image larger than 30,000 x 30,000 pixels and preserve the layer-based edits theyve made to that image, they must save the image as a PSB file. The PSB file format is designed specifically to allow Photoshop users to save large Photoshop documents, whether the document is large in actual size or file size. Images larger than 2 GB in file size must also be saved as PSB files, regardless of how many pixels they contain. PSB files contain the same types of image, text, edit, and effect layers as PSD files. In fact, the PSB file format is roughly identical to the PSD file format, except that the PSB format supports larger images. However, the PSB format is not supported by as many programs as the PSD format, which means you may have trouble opening a PSB file outside of Photoshop and other Adobe programs. NOTE: PSB files can contain images that are up to 300,000 x 300,000 pixels in size. Photoshop does not allow users to create images larger than 300,000 x 300,000 pixels. You can open a PSB file in Adobe Photoshop in Windows and macOS. To open a PSB file, select File → Open.., then choose the PSB file. In macOS, you can preview the image a PSB file contains with the Quick Look feature (by selecting your PSB file and pressing your spacebar). Web File Helper. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Movie subtitles file created for use with PowerDivX, an older multimedia player; saves subtitles in a simple text format, specifying the start and stop time of each subtitle; for example:. {0:01:21}{0:01:51}My Movie Subtitle 1. {0:01:21}{0:01:51}My Movie Subtitle 1. The PSB format is still supported by VLC media player. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Any text editor Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Any text editor Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Any text editor.",
    "Web File Helper. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Any text editor. Windows VideoLAN VLC media player. Any text editor. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Any text editor.",
    "Adobe Photoshop can convert PSB files to the following formats:.PSD - Adobe Photoshop Document.PSDC - Adobe Photoshop Cloud Document.PDF - Portable Document Format.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.WEBP - WebP Image.AI - Adobe Illustrator Artwork.BMP - Bitmap Image.DCM - DICOM Image.EPS - Encapsulated PostScript.TGA - Targa Graphic."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".APNG",
    "Animated Portable Network Graphic",
    "3.6",
    "Unofficial extension to the Animated Portable Network Graphic (APNG) format; contains multiple frames (.PNG images) used for an animation sequence; similar to an animated.GIF file, but also supports 24-bit images and 8-bit transparency. Since the initial frame in a APNG file is stored as a normal PNG image, animated PNGs are backwards compatible with many applications that support PNG files. APNG files commonly use the standard .png extension. Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. XnViewMP. Opera. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome with APNG extension. Bandisoft Honeyview. Mac XnViewMP. Opera. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome with APNG extension. Linux Opera. Mozilla Firefox. KSquirrel —  (Discontinued). Google Chrome with APNG extensionFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. XnViewMP. Opera. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome with APNG extension. Bandisoft Honeyview. Mac XnViewMP. Opera. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome with APNG extension. Linux Opera. Mozilla Firefox. KSquirrel —  (Discontinued). Google Chrome with APNG extension.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PTG",
    "ArtRage Painting",
    "3.6",
    "Configuration file used by PowerTeacher Gradebook, a web-based classroom management application; contains grade book configuration information that is referenced when the application connects to the server; includes user id, session id, school number, teacher id, credentials, and language. Windows Pearson Education PowerTeacher Gradebook. Mac Pearson Education PowerTeacher Gradebook. Paint project with ArtRage, an image editing and painting program; contains all project image data saved in ArtRage; can be exported to other image file types, including.PNG,.JPG, and.PSD; can be displayed as a thumbnail in Windows and Mac OS X. ArtRage is available in standard and Studio Pro editions. Windows Ambient Design ArtRage Studio. Mac Ambient Design ArtRage Studio.",
    "Windows Pearson Education PowerTeacher Gradebook. Mac Pearson Education PowerTeacher Gradebook. Windows Ambient Design ArtRage Studio. Mac Ambient Design ArtRage Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".ASEPRITE",
    "Aseprite Sprite File",
    "3.6",
    "An ASEPRITE file contains a sprite created by Aseprite, an animated sprite editor and pixel art tool. It stores a graphic or animation, which includes layers, frames, palettes, and tags. ASEPRITE files also contain sprite settings, such as the width, height, color mode, pixel aspect ration, and background. ASEPRITE file open in Aseprite 1.2 ASEPRITE files may also be saved as.ASE files, which are saved in the same format but with a different extension. ASEPRITE and ASE files are the most common files associated with Aseprite and can be closed and re-opened for further editing in the program. You can create an ASEPRITE file in Aseprite by selecting File → New.., then File → Save or Save As.., and choosing the ASEPRITE format. You can open an ASEPRITE file in Aseprite by selecting File → Open.. or Open Recent and choosing the ASEPRITE file. Aseprite can also be used to export ASEPRITE files to more popular formats, such as.PNG or.GIF files. With the ASEPRITE file open, select File → Save Copy As. Windows Aseprite. Mac Aseprite. Linux Aseprite.",
    "Windows Aseprite. Mac Aseprite. Linux Aseprite.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".AWD",
    "Microsoft Fax Document",
    "3.6",
    "An AWD file is a raster image created by Microsoft Fax, also known as Microsoft at Work Fax. It contains a copy of a document a user received via Microsoft Fax. AWD files are sometimes referred to as At Work Documents. Microsoft Fax was part of Windows Messaging, an email client included with Windows 95 and available for Windows 98. It allowed users to send and receive faxes. The program saved copies of received faxes as AWD files. Each AWD file contains the text and page structure information needed to display a faxed document in Microsoft Fax. You can open an AWD file with Polybytes PolyView (Windows). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your AWD file. Windows Polybytes PolyView —  (Discontinued). Updater file used to update or flash the BIOS of a Windows PC; typically used for updating ASUS motherboards that use the Award BIOS. NOTE: In some cases, the AWD file extension may need to be changed to.BIN in order to be loaded by the AWDFLASH program. Windows ASUS AWDFLASH. Drawing created with Artweaver, a creative painting program designed to simulate natural brush tools; may include sketches created with several types of brushes and many different colors; supports image transparency, text, and layers. Windows Boris Eyrich Artweaver. XnViewMP with the AWD pluginFree.",
    "Windows Polybytes PolyView —  (Discontinued). Windows ASUS AWDFLASH. Windows Boris Eyrich Artweaver. XnViewMP with the AWD plugin.",
    "You can use Polybytes PolyView to convert AWD files to many other image formats, including:.BMP - Bitmap Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.JPEG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".BMQ",
    "Re-Volt Mipmap File",
    "3.6",
    "Mipmap image used by Re-Volt, an old RC car racing game for the PC; contains a low-resolution image in the BMP format that is used for object textures viewed from afar in the game in order to keep the frame rate stable. Mipmaps are used by Re-Volt to improve texture rendering during gameplay. They are used for textures that are viewed from a distance and dont require large images for detail. If the main texture size is 256x256, the next mipmap image would be 128x128, then 64x64, and then 32x32 after that. Once the camera gets closer to the object texture the BMQ mipmap is replaced with the normal BMP image. By using smaller images, the games rendering speed is increased. Windows Acclaim Entertainment Re-Volt. Microsoft Paint Included with OS.",
    "Windows Acclaim Entertainment Re-Volt. Microsoft Paint Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".JNG",
    "JPEG Network Graphic",
    "3.5",
    "A JNG file is an image saved in the JPEG Network Graphic (JNG) format. Like.PNG images, JNG images can contain transparent sections. However, like.JPG images, JNG images are compressed using lossy compression. JNG file open in XnViewMP The PNG Development Group created the JNG format for use alongside the.MNG format. JNG files often contain a still image that is a single frame of an MNG animation. Unlike typical PNG files, JNG files are compressed using lossy compression. For this reason, they may be subject to the blurring and other distortions that sometimes affect JPG files, and they also typically have smaller file sizes than similar PNG files. The image data a JNG file contains is encoded using JPEG compression and stored in a PNG container. Like PNG files, JNG files can contain an alpha channel that allows them to include transparent sections. However, not all JNG files contain an alpha channel or transparent sections. You can open a JNG file with ImageMagick (multiplatform), XnViewMP (multiplatform), or IrfanView (Windows). Web File Helper. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. XnViewMP. ImageMagick. IrfanView. Mac XnViewMP. ImageMagick. Linux XnViewMP. ImageMagickFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. XnViewMP. ImageMagick. IrfanView. Mac XnViewMP. ImageMagick. Linux XnViewMP. ImageMagick.",
    "You can use ImageMagick or XnViewMP to convert JNG files to other image formats. For example, XnViewMP can convert JNG files to the following formats (and many others):.JPEG - JPEG Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.JP2 - JPEG 2000 Core Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image.WEBP - WebP Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PPM",
    "Portable Pixmap Image",
    "3.5",
    "A PPM file is a raster image saved in the Portable Pixmap format. It contains plain text that specifies the images type (plain or raw), its number of columns and rows, and its maximum color value. Plain PPM files then specify each pixels color using ASCII-encoded numbers, while raw PPM files specify each included pixels color using raw binary data. PPM file open in XnViewMP In the late 1980s, developer Jef Poskanzer created the PPM image format and added tools that could create and read PPM images to Pbmplus, his library of tools used to create and manage.PBM,.PGM, and PPM images. PPM files contain color images saved using an RGB color model. Typically, the images use a 24-bit color depth. In most PPM files, each pixels color is specified using a trio of ASCII numbers that set the pixels red, green, and blue color values. Image rows are comprised of sets of RGB values equal to the images width. These types of PPM files are referred to as plain PPM files and can be identified by the magic number P3 in their header. Raw PPM files, on the other hand, specify each pixels color using raw binary data, instead of ASCII-encoded numbers. If you were to open a raw PPM file in a text editor, its body would appear as gibberish instead of an understandable series of numbers. These files include the magic number P6 in their header. While many programs support the PPM format, PPM images have quite large file sizes when compared with images saved in other formats, because they are not compressed. Thus, the PPM format is not used much. You can open a PPM file with many image viewing and editing programs. For example, you can open a PPM file with GIMP (multiplatform), XnViewMP (multiplatform), or Netpbm (multiplatform). Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus. GIMP. ImageMagick. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. ImageMagick. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Android File Viewer for Android. Data file used to flash some Nokia mobile phones; sometimes used to change the language pack on a phone to support a different language; may also use the.PPM_B, PPM_C, or PPM_D file extensions. Windows BB5 FLS Editor. A PPM file is an animation created by Flipnote Studio, a free animation app available for the Nintendo DSi. It contains animation frames and audio. PPM files are typically stored on a Nintendo DSi SD card. Flipnote Studio is an animation app that Nintendo DSi players can download from the DSi Shop. It allows gamers to create simple animations and save them to their DSIs SD cards. These animations are saved as PPM files. PPM files are typically stored in the following locations: North America: /​private/​ds/​app/​4B475545/​001 Europe: /​private/​ds/​app/​4B475556/​001 Some players have uploaded their PPM files to online Flipnote repositories, such as Flipnote Hatena or PPM Archive, from which other Flipnote users can download them. NOTE: The PPM extension comes from Flipnote Studios in-development name, Para Para Manga Koubou. In addition to being able to open and play PPM files in Flipnote Studio, you can open them in the web-based Flipnote Player. Web Flipnote PlayerFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus. GIMP. ImageMagick. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. ImageMagick. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows BB5 FLS Editor. Web Flipnote Player.",
    "You can use Netpbm, ImageMagick or XnViewMP to convert PPM files to other image formats. For example, XnViewMP can convert PPM files to the following formats (and many others):.JPG - JPEG Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.JP2 - JPEG 2000 Core Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image.WEBP - WebP Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".TIF",
    "Tagged Image File",
    "3.5",
    "A TIF file is an image saved in the Tagged Image File Format (TIFF), a high-quality graphics format. It is often used for storing images with many colors, typically digital photos, and includes support for layers and multiple pages. TIF file open in Microsoft Photos 2020 The TIFF format was developed in the mid-1980s by Aldus Corporation (merged with Adobe Systems in 1994) to be a universal image format for different computer platforms and document scanners. The format became popular among professionals in the publishing industry, including photographers and graphic artists. The formats popularity was partially due to its ability to be edited and re-saved without losing image quality. TIF files can be saved in an uncompressed (lossless) format or may incorporate.JPEG (lossy) compression. They may also use LZW lossless compression, which reduces the TIF file size but does not reduce the quality of the image. NOTE: TIF files may also use the.TIFF extension. You can open a TIF file with various image editors since the TIFF format is common among graphics professionals. Some applications that support the format include Microsoft Photos (Windows), CorelDRAW Graphics Suite (Windows and macOS), ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio (Windows), Adobe Photoshop (Windows and macOS), and Apple Preview (bundled with macOS). NOTE: You can also open TIF files with Google Photos in a web browser, Chrome OS, and on Android and iOS devices. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Illustrator 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Apple Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Illustrator 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio for Mac. MacPhun ColorStrokes. Linux GIMP. Web Apple Photos Included with OS. Google Photos. Google Drive. iOS Apple Photos Included with OS. Google Photos. Google Drive. Android File Viewer for Android. Google Photos. Google Drive. Chrome OS Google PhotosFree. A TIF file is a TIFF-compliant geospatial image created in the GeoTIFF format. It contains geographic or cartographic data embedded as tags within the file. TIF files allow users to embed GIS data without deviating from the TIFF (Tagged Image File Format) format. TIF file open in QGIS 3 Since GeoTIFF files contain coordinates, GIS applications can map specific regions of the raster image to latitude and longitude coordinates. NOTE: The GeoTIFF format uses the extensible features of the TIFF specification to add tagged metadata to the image. You can open a TIF file in ESRI ArcGIS Pro (Windows), OriginLab Origin (Windows), QGIS (multiplatform), and several other GIS applications. You can also open a TIF file in any image viewer that can open normal TIF files (such as Microsoft Photos or Apple Preview). However, image viewers will not show the geographic data your TIF file contains. Windows Geosoft Oasis montaj. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. The MathWorks MATLAB. ERDAS IMAGINE. QGIS. GDAL. OriginLab Origin. Mac QGIS. ClueTrust Cartographica. GDAL. ERDAS ER Viewer —  (Discontinued). Linux QGIS. GDALFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Illustrator 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Apple Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. Adobe Lightroom. Adobe Illustrator 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio for Mac. MacPhun ColorStrokes. Linux GIMP. Web Apple Photos Included with OS. Google Photos. Google Drive. iOS Apple Photos Included with OS. Google Photos. Google Drive. Android File Viewer for Android. Google Photos. Google Drive. Chrome OS Google Photos. Windows Geosoft Oasis montaj. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. The MathWorks MATLAB. ERDAS IMAGINE. QGIS. GDAL. OriginLab Origin. Mac QGIS. ClueTrust Cartographica. GDAL. ERDAS ER Viewer —  (Discontinued). Linux QGIS. GDAL.",
    "Several image viewers and editors, including Microsoft Photos, Apple Preview, and Adobe Photoshop, can convert TIF files to other image formats. For example, Microsoft Photos can convert TIF files to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.BMP - Bitmap Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".THM",
    "Video Thumbnail File",
    "3.5",
    "A THM file is a theme file used by Sony Ericsson mobile phones. It stores settings used to customize the user interface of the cell phone and includes custom window and text colors, icons, wallpaper, and other images. THM files can be created and edited using the free Themes Creator from Sony Ericsson, which is no longer developed. Windows Sony Ericsson Themes Creator Mac Sony Ericsson Themes Creator. A THM file is a thumbnail image generated by digital camcorders and software programs when saving a video clip. It contains a small image from the video clips first frame and is displayed to help a user identify a clip when visually browsing through a collection of video clips. THM files often are saved in the JPEG format. When you are capturing video with a digital camcorder or camera, the device creates a thumbnail of the video and saves it to its memory card or internal storage. Then, when you import video from a camcorder or camera, the software you are using to transfer the video also transfers the associated THM files. Each THM file transferred from a device to a computer shares the same filename as its associated video clip. For example, a THM file for clip001.avi is created as clip001.thm. You will likely never need to open a THM file since the software program you use to browse video clips displays the thumbnail image next to the video clip. However, if you encounter a THM file and need to open it individually, you can attempt to open it directly with an image viewer, such as Microsoft Photos, Microsoft Paint, or Apple Preview. If that does not work, you can change the.thm file extension to.jpg and attempt again to open it with an image viewer. NOTE: If the THM file is not saved in JPEG format, you will likely be unable to open it with an image editor. Windows Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. Microsoft Paint Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Sony Picture Motion Browser —  (Discontinued). Other image viewer Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer Linux Any image viewer. Macro file used by Thermwood CNC Routers; contains router machining instructions that automate router processes; a list of CNC events are also saved in a file named hist.thm.. Windows Thermwood Mastercam. A THM file is a thumbnail image, which is a small, icon-sized image that represents a larger image. It is saved in a bitmap format similar to a.JPG file but at a lower resolution. Digital camera and photo or video-editing apps often create THM files to store small previews of larger images and videos. THM file open in Apple Preview 11 The purpose of THM thumbnails is to provide a quick preview that gives you an idea of the image, video, clip art, etc., you are browsing. Since the thumbnail is saved at such a low resolution, it is not meant to be opened and viewed the same as the original file for which it stores the preview. You can open THM files with various image viewers and editors, such as Microsoft Photos (Windows) and Apple Preview (Mac). For example, to open a THM file with Preview, select File → Open. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. A THM file is a raster image saved in the GoPro Thumbnail format. It stores image data similar to the JPEG format but also contains GoPro-specific metadata, including the date and time it was captured and the settings of the camera. GoPro cameras, such as the HERO2 and HERO3, automatically generate THM thumbnail images from captured footage to help users preview images and video. Select GoPro cameras create THM and.LRV files to accompany captured footage to aid you as you browse through your footage on the camera screen or your mobile phone (using the Quik app). For example, a GoPro HERO2 user will find a THM and LRV file next to their.MP4 video. The THM file is a small preview (typically 160x120) created from a single frame in your footage that is also small in size to allow for quicker loading times as you scroll. Additionally, the LRV file is a low-resolution video utilized during the editing process to reduce the amount of computing power required to edit a video. Deleting GoPro THM files You can delete THM files to remove clutter, but it may affect the speed at which you can preview footage on the camera or in the Quik app. However, the actual footage will not be affected. GOPR0[numbered video].THM - GoPro cameras name the THM file after the MP4 file it accompanies. For example, if you just recorded the 120th video, GoPro names the MP4 video GOPR0120.MP4 and the thumbnail GOPR0120.THM. THM files are not meant to be manually opened. Instead, GoPro cameras and the Quik app (iOS and Android) reference them for quicker loading times as you browse through footage. However, since the files are saved in a JPEG format, you may be able to view them with an app that supports JPEG images. iOS GoPro Quik. Android GoPro Quik.",
    "Windows Sony Ericsson Themes Creator. Mac Sony Ericsson Themes Creator. Windows Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. Microsoft Paint Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Sony Picture Motion Browser —  (Discontinued). Other image viewer. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer. Linux Any image viewer. Windows Thermwood Mastercam. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. iOS GoPro Quik. Android GoPro Quik.",
    "If the THM file is saved in JPEG format, you can convert it to other formats with many image editors, including Microsoft Paint, Adobe Photoshop, and Apple Preview. For example, Paint can convert THM files saved in JPEG format to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.JFIF - JPEG File Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.HEIC - High Efficiency Image Format.DIB - Device Independent Bitmap. Apple Preview and Microsoft Photos can convert THM files to other formats. For example, Preview can convert THM files to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.EXR - OpenEXR Image.HEIC - High Efficiency Image Format.PDF - Portable Document Format."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".CPT",
    "Corel PHOTO-PAINT Image",
    "3.5",
    "A CPT file is a bitmap image created by Corel PHOTO-PAINT, a photo editing program included with CorelDRAW Graphics Suite. It contains an image that supports layers, alpha channels, transparency, and other effects. CPT files are the native files PHOTO-PAINT saves to store images users create or modify with the software. CPT file open in Corel PHOTO-PAINT 2023 Amateur and professional photographers and graphic designers may use Corel PHOTO-PAINT to create or edit images for various purposes. Examples include advertisements, photo collages, social media and web graphics, and artistic illustrations. When you save an image with PHOTO-PAINT, the application creates the CPT file, by default, to store the image and all the edits you have applied. After saving the CPT file, you can close it and re-open it to apply future edits. How to create a CPT file with PHOTO-PAINT To create a CPT file with PHOTO-PAINT: Select File → New. Name the file, choose the dimensions and other settings, then click OK. Edit the image. Select File → Save or Save As, choose the save location, and click Save. You can open a CPT file with the Corel PHOTO-PAINT application included with CorelDRAW Graphics Suite (Windows and macOS). To open a CPT file with PHOTO-PAINT, select File → Open. You can also open CPT files with Corel Presentations (Windows) and XnViewMP (multiplatform). Mac CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. XnViewMP. Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Corel Presentations 2021. XnViewMP. Chasys Draw IESFree. File archive encrypted with ccrypt, a utility for encrypting and decrypting files and streams; based on the Rijndael cipher and uses an asymmetric encryption algorithm; requires a password to open. Ccrypt is developed as an open-source program and is available for Mac, Windows, and Unix systems. Mac ccrypt Windows ccrypt Linux ccrypt. File archive compressed with Compact Pro, a file compression program for Mac OS Classic (Mac OS 9 and earlier); uses a fast and efficient compression algorithm. Development of Compact Pro stopped in the late 1990s and the program is no longer supported. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. The Unarchiver. Cyclos Compact Pro (Mac OS Classic). Audio file used by DVD authoring programs; contains audio, timecode, and header data; used in conjunction with video data to create DVDs. NOTE: CPT files cannot be used to author Blu-ray discs. The.DTSHD format can be used instead. Mac DTS-HD Master Audio Suite DTS Surround Audio Suite Apple DVD Studio Pro. SurCode DTS-HD Encoder for Compressor Windows DTS-HD Master Audio Suite DTS Surround Audio Suite. Presentation created by Conduits Pocket Slides on a Pocket PC PDA. Windows Microsoft ActiveSyncFree.",
    "Mac CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. XnViewMP. Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Corel Presentations 2021. XnViewMP. Chasys Draw IES. Mac ccrypt. Windows ccrypt. Linux ccrypt. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. The Unarchiver. Cyclos Compact Pro (Mac OS Classic). Mac DTS-HD Master Audio Suite DTS Surround Audio Suite Apple DVD Studio Pro. SurCode DTS-HD Encoder for Compressor. Windows DTS-HD Master Audio Suite DTS Surround Audio Suite. Windows Microsoft ActiveSync.",
    "Several applications, including CorelDRAW Graphics Suite and XnViewMP, can convert CPT files to various formats. For example, the PHOTO-PAINT application included with CorelDRAW Graphics Suite can convert CPT files to many file types, including the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.BMP - Bitmap Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.TGA - Targa Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.WEBP - WebP Image.EPS - Encapsulated PostScript File.PSD - Adobe Photoshop Document.PDF - Portable Document Format."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".CAN",
    "Canvas Painting",
    "3.5",
    "Fax document saved from a Canon fax machine or all-in-one printer/copier/scanner/fax device; may be generated by Canon Navigator, the software included with Canon fax machines. NOTE: Canon Navigator for multifunction devices is now called MP Navigator. Windows Canon MP Navigator XnViewMP. Mac Canon MP Navigator XnViewMPFree. A CAN file is a digital painting created using NVIDIA Canvas. It contains one image that is comprised of simple brushstrokes and another image that is a realistic landscape. Canvas uses AI to generate the realistic landscape from the brushstrokes. CAN file open in Adobe Photoshop 2022 Users whose Windows computers use an NVIDIA RTX GPU can install NVIDIA Canvas and use it to create digital landscape paintings. To create a painting, users paint a series of simple brushstrokes on a canvas. Each brushstroke corresponds to a landscape element, such as the sky, clouds, plants, or water bodies. Canvas then uses its AI to transform these brushstrokes into a coherent, realistic-looking landscape. Users can select from several landscape styles, to create many different types of landscapes (e.g. deserts, coastal landscapes, etc.) Paintings created using Canvas are saved as CAN files. Each CAN file contains a record of all the paintings brushstrokes and layers and the most recent landscaping style applied to the painting. You can open a CAN file in NVIDIA Canvas (Windows). To do so, select the Open icon that appears in Canvass menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your CAN file. You can also open a CAN file in Adobe Photoshop (Windows, Mac). When you do, Photoshop loads the AI-generated landscape image the file contains as a Background layer, and the brushstrokes the file contains as one or more additional layers. Windows NVIDIA Canvas. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023.",
    "Windows Canon MP Navigator XnViewMP. Mac Canon MP Navigator XnViewMP. Windows NVIDIA Canvas. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023.",
    "You can use NVIDIA Canvas to convert CAN files to the following formats:.PSD - Adobe Photoshop Document.PNG - Portable Network Graphic."],
