    "Graphic Object Bitmap",
    "3.3",
    "Bitmap image format sometimes referred to as a GROB (GRaphic Object Bitmap); used by Hewlett-Packard scientific calculators, such as the HP-48 and HP-49; used for storing graphs, charts, and other graphics created on the calculator. GRO files may be viewed on a computer using a supporting HP calculator emulator, such as Emu48. Windows Emu48. XnViewMP. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Mac Emu48. XnViewMPFree. ASCII text file that defines audio in a MIDI representation; also contains note tracks, which specify display data for the audio; can be imported (and subsequently converted to other audio formats) using Audacitys File → Import MIDI.. option. Windows Audacity. Mac Audacity. Linux AudacityFree.",
