    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PANO",
    "Camera Panoramic Picture",
    "2.9",
    "File created by Windows Camera, a photo and video recording application; contains a photo generated from several different images taken from the same vantage point and stitched together by the Camera application. To create a PANO file: Open your Camera application, line up where you want your first photo taken and select the Panorama button, which will capture your first image. Slowly move the camera to line up your next picture with the one you just took and it will automatically capture the next photo. Repeat step 2 until youve completed the panorama view and click the check mark, this will create your PANO file. NOTE: The PANO file was released with Windows 8.1 and is not compatible with earlier operating systems. Windows Microsoft Camera Microsoft OneDrive.",
    "Windows Microsoft Camera Microsoft OneDrive.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".ZVI",
    "Zeiss Vision Image",
    "2.9",
    "A ZVI file is an image saved in the Zeiss Vision Image (ZVI) format. It contains a high-resolution image captured by a Zeiss microscope that supports up to 3x16-bit color and 16-bit monochrome. ZVI files also include metadata, such as camera and microscope settings. ZVI files are created by AxioVision, a program used to capture images from a Zeiss microscope. The software not only allows you to capture images but also to analyze the properties of materials structures. You can also export ZVI images to.JPG,.TIF,.TGA,.PNG,.AVI,.MOV,.CMP,.J2K, and.BMP files. AxioVision is mainly used in the scientific field by metallurgists. You can open a ZVI file with Carl Zeiss AxioVision (Windows) or NetScope Viewer (Windows). Windows Carl Zeiss AxioVision —  (Discontinued). NetScope Viewer.",
    "Windows Carl Zeiss AxioVision —  (Discontinued). NetScope Viewer.",
    "You can use Carl Zeiss AxioVision (Windows) or NetScope Viewer (Windows) to convert the image a ZVI file contains to other formats. For example, NetScope Viewer can convert ZVI files to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format."],
