    ["raster_image_files",
    ".SMP",
    "Xionics SMP Image",
    "2.3",
    "An SMP file is an encrypted.MP3 file that can be found on a memory card used by a Salvat AudioCuentos or Märchenheld Sammlung audio player. It contains a childrens audiobook. SMP files can be played only by AudioCuentos and Märchenheld audio players. Both Salvat AudioCuentos and Märchenheld offer a series of childrens audiobooks that are played by placing a figurine atop a square, blue audio player (sometimes referred to as an audio cube). The audio player contains a memory card that stores a number of SMP files, each of which contains an audiobook. When a child places a figurine atop the audio player, the player loads and plays that figurines associated SMP file. In most circumstances, those who use AudioCuentos and Märchenheld audiobooks should never have to encounter or manually open an SMP file. The only way you would encounter an SMP file is if you removed the memory card from an AudioCuentos or Märchenheld audio player and connected it to your computer. You cannot open or play an SMP audiobook file on a computer or mobile device. You can, however, convert an SMP file to an MP3 file using audiocube.py (cross-platform) or SMP2MP3 (Windows). Then, you can play the MP3 file in most media players. The only way to natively play an SMP file is to place it on a memory card, place the memory card within an AudioCuentos or Märchenheld audio player, and then place the SMP files associated figurine atop the player. Windows SMP2MP3. audiocube.py. Mac audiocube.py. Linux audiocube.pyFree. An SMP file is a ScrapeMap created by skyLyn Applications ScrapeMate, a program used to scrape information from websites and organize it in a database or spreadsheet. It stores information about the targeted data and how it should be organized and stored after it is scraped. ScrapeMate is an application that makes it easier to collect information from websites and save it in a format you can view and modify. Unfortunately, skyLyn Applications no longer develops the software. How to create an SMP file with ScrapeMate You can create a ScrapeMap with ScrapeMate using the ScrapeMap Explorer pane. First, you choose the website to scrape, filter and sort the data you want to target, click the Create ScrapeMap icon, and choose the save location of the file. ScrapeMate then saves the ScrapeMap as an SMP file. You will also be prompted to choose the output format of the data scraped from the website. For example, you can choose to export the data to Excel (.XLSX file), CSV (.CSV file), or SQL (.SQL file). You can open a ScrapeMap SMP file with ScrapeMate via the ScrapeMap Explorer pane. In the pane, click the Open ScrapeMap folder icon and navigate to the location of the SMP file. Windows skyLyn Applications ScrapeMate —  (Discontinued). Trial. An SMP file is a data file created by SmilePlant, a Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS) that helps plant administrators with supervision, management, and maintenance. It stores information about plant equipment, employees, and production and storage areas. SMP files are saved as one of a set of files in the SmilePlant project folder. SmilePlant has been discontinued and is no longer maintained. Windows Stellar Solutions SmilePlant. Music file used by SmartMusic, a music practice application for band, orchestra, and voice; saves an accompaniment that can be used for practicing solos and other musical parts; includes the sheet music information and can be used for assessment; replaced by the.SMPX in Finale 2014. NOTE: SMP files can be exported from Finale musical notation software. Windows MakeMusic SmartMusic. Mac MakeMusic SmartMusic. Color palette file created by IDRISI Taiga, an application used for GIS imaging; stores color information for a raster image stored in a.RST file; acts as a legend for the colors displayed when the image is visualized. Windows Clark Labs TerrSet. GDAL. Linux GDALFree. Mono, 16-bit audio format that supports loop points; originally used by Turtle Beach SampleVision in the mid-1990s. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. MAGIX Sound Forge Pro 16. FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Image used by Xionics Document Technologies software; stores a monochrome (black and white) 1-bit raster graphic; can still be viewed and converted with a few programs even though the file format is rare. Windows Cheewoo Engineering VaryView XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMPFree. An SMP file is a gallery file created by Ulead PhotoImpact (now Corel PhotoImpact), a program used to edit photos and digital art. It contains a gallery, which may include images, objects, image enhancements, or text/animation effects. SMP files also include gallery properties such as the number of tab groups, number of thumbnails, and size of the file. Galleries allow you to store different effects, enhancements, or images then apply them to your artwork. The SMP file is created when you select Create from the Gallery Manager in EasyPalette, name the file, choose the save location, and click OK. You can also create an SMP file by selecting Export. You can load an SMP Gallery file by selecting Load.. in the Gallery Manager. Windows Corel PhotoImpact.",
    "Windows SMP2MP3. audiocube.py. Mac audiocube.py. Linux audiocube.py. Windows skyLyn Applications ScrapeMate —  (Discontinued). Trial. Windows Stellar Solutions SmilePlant. Windows MakeMusic SmartMusic. Mac MakeMusic SmartMusic. Windows Clark Labs TerrSet. GDAL. Linux GDAL. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. MAGIX Sound Forge Pro 16. FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Windows Cheewoo Engineering VaryView XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Windows Corel PhotoImpact.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".POV",
    "Prolab Object File",
    "2.3",
    "Three-dimensional graphic that uses the Persistence of Vision Raytracer (POV-Ray) format; supports shapes, colors, textures, rotations, light, atmospheric effects, viewing perspectives, and other 3D image properties; stored in an ASCII text format. POV files are defined using the POV-Ray scene description language, which specifies instructions for how the POV-Ray engine renders 3D graphics. POV files can be used for rendering high-quality photorealistic images. POV-Ray is a free program available for Mac, Windows, and Unix platforms. Windows POV-Ray. Mac POV-Ray. Linux POV-RayFree. Graphic format used by Prolab ImageFolio, an older image editing program that was distributed with VideoWork and MediaScope software; stores an image that supports layers. Windows VideoLogic Prolab ImageFolio.",
    "Windows POV-Ray. Mac POV-Ray. Linux POV-Ray. Windows VideoLogic Prolab ImageFolio.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".DDB",
    "Device Dependent Bitmap",
    "2.3",
    "Application support file created by Pro Tools, a digital audio workstation (DAW) application; contains application support information for an audio project and uses the filename volume.ddb. NOTE: Digidesign is now Avid Technology. Windows Avid Pro Tools. Mac Avid Pro Tools. Game file used by Command & Conquer: Renegade, a third-person shooter game; saves game data such as player abilities and weapons; sometimes used by the gaming community to create custom modifications that alter gameplay and game properties. DDB files are often named objects.ddb and are located in the /​Renegade/​Data/​ directory. Windows Westwood Studios Command & Conquer Renegade. Bitmap image formatted for a specific device driver, such as a video card driver; saved in a proprietary format defined by the video card manufacturer. DDB files are not meant to be opened manually, though they may be viewed with a supporting third-party image editor. Windows Not meant to be opened Mac Not meant to be opened.",
    "Windows Avid Pro Tools. Mac Avid Pro Tools. Windows Westwood Studios Command & Conquer Renegade. Windows Not meant to be opened. Mac Not meant to be opened.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".RVG",
    "RVG X-ray Image",
    "2.3",
    "Image format used by dental radiography systems developed by Kodak; created by dental imaging sensors to store x-ray images of a patients mouth. There are several editions of the Kodak RVG software, including 6500, 6200, 6100, and 5100. Trophy RVG Mobile program can only be used to view RVG images taken by the Kodak RVG 6500 program. NOTE: Kodak RVG is discontinued. Windows Kodak RVG Aeskulap. Linux AeskulapFree.",
    "Windows Kodak RVG Aeskulap. Linux Aeskulap.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".SGI",
    "Silicon Graphics Image",
    "2.3",
    "An SGI file is an image saved in the Silicon Graphics Image (SGI) format. It is typically a color image, shown using three color channels. SGI files contain images that were meant to be shown on Silicon Graphics workstations. SGI file open in XnViewMP Silicon Graphics Inc., also known as SGI, was a computer and software company that was founded in 1981 and went bankrupt in 2009. SGI developer Paul Haeberli created the SGI image format in 1995. Many of the workstations Silicon Graphics produced used the SGI format as their native graphics format. Each SGI image can store 8 to 32 bits per pixel. The format also supports run-length encoding (RLE) compression, which reduces each images file size. SGI images are also saved as.RGB files. SGI images that include an alpha channel may be saved as.RGBA files. You can open an SGI file in many image viewers and editors, including File Viewer Plus (Windows), Apple Preview (Mac), XnViewMP (Windows, Mac), and qView (multiplatform). Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. qView. Android File Viewer for Android.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. qView. Android File Viewer for Android.",
    "Most image viewers and editors that can open SGI files can convert them to other image formats. For example, XnViewMP can convert SGI files to the following formats (and many others):.JPEG - JPEG Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.JP2 - JPEG 2000 Core Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image.WEBP - WebP Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".SPU",
    "Spectrum 512 Image",
    "2.3",
    "Bitmap image originally created by Spectrum 512, a graphics application that ran on the Atari ST systems; supports bitmap graphics with up to 512 colors; may still be opened using some image viewing programs. Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Atari Picture Viewer XnViewMP. Mac Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Atari Picture Viewer XnViewMP. Mac Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".OMF",
    "OMF Interchange Image File",
    "2.3",
    "An OMF file is an audio file saved in a standard audio/video format based on the Open Media Framework Interchange (OMFI), a standardized interchange file format. It may be exported from digital video editing or audio workstation (DAW) software and is commonly used to share project data between multiple applications. An audio project saved in the OMF format can store multiple audio tracks, volume and pan information, and references to audio files. However, not all settings, such as insertion effects and channel routing options, may be saved in an OMF file. Therefore, not all project and track settings may be transferred when opening an OMF file in another application. Windows Avid Media Composer. Avid Pro Tools. Steinberg Cubase. Cakewalk SONAR X3. MOTU Digital Performer. Adobe Audition 2023. Mac Avid Media Composer. Avid Pro Tools. Steinberg Cubase. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Pro. MOTU Digital Performer. Adobe Audition 2023. Image file based on the OMF (Open Media Framework) standard; designed for storing image data in a standardized format that can be viewed on multiple systems and platforms. Windows Equilibrium DeBabelizer Mac Equilibrium DeBabelizer.",
    "Windows Avid Media Composer. Avid Pro Tools. Steinberg Cubase. Cakewalk SONAR X3. MOTU Digital Performer. Adobe Audition 2023. Mac Avid Media Composer. Avid Pro Tools. Steinberg Cubase. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Pro. MOTU Digital Performer. Adobe Audition 2023. Windows Equilibrium DeBabelizer. Mac Equilibrium DeBabelizer.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".RRI",
    "RealWorld Image",
    "2.3",
    "Image format used by RealWorld Graphics products such as RealWorld Icon Editor and RealWorld Cursor Editor; saves a raster image that was edited in the software, but uses a proprietary format that can only be opened in RealWorld Graphics programs; used for making Windows icon and cursor graphics. RRI images are less common than RealWorld Layered Images (.RLI), since the RRI format only supports a single editing layer while the RLI format supports multiple layers. Recent versions of Cursor Editor can open files in the RRI format, but it cannot save them. Windows RealWorld Icon Editor. RealWorld Cursor EditorFree.",
    "Windows RealWorld Icon Editor. RealWorld Cursor Editor.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PNM",
    "Portable Any Map Image",
    "2.2",
    "Bitmap image created in the Portable Any Map format, which was designed to handle several types of portable monochrome, grayscale, and color images; may include raster graphic data in a.PBM,.PGM, or.PPM format; may be stored using binary data or ASCII text. PNM files store one image and do not use compression. Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. ImageMagick. XnViewMP. GIMP. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac ImageMagick. XnViewMP. GIMP. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Linux ImageMagick. XnViewMP. GIMPFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. ImageMagick. XnViewMP. GIMP. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac ImageMagick. XnViewMP. GIMP. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Linux ImageMagick. XnViewMP. GIMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".JBG",
    "Joint Bi-level Image Group File",
    "2.2",
    "Image format used to store black and white, grayscale, and color images; uses lossless compression to create smaller image file sizes than other industry standard formats, such as CCITT Group 3 (G3) or CCITT Group 4 (G4) compression. The Joint Bi-level Image Group (JBIG) format, also called JBIG1, was intended for compressing binary images, mainly for fax transmissions, but can also be used for other images. It was replaced by the JBIG2 specification (.JB2 files), which compresses bi-level images more efficiently. NOTE: Images saved in the JBIG format also use the more common.JBIG file extension. Mac Newera Graphics Converter Pro. ToyViewer. XnViewMP. Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. XnViewMPFree.",
    "Mac Newera Graphics Converter Pro. ToyViewer. XnViewMP. Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".YUV",
    "YUV Encoded Image File",
    "2.2",
    "A YUV file is a video file encoded in the YUV format. It stores a sequence of YUV images as a single video file and may be saved in YUV 4:2:0, 4:2:2, 4:4:4 formats. YUV video files may be decoded by MPEG-4 and H.264 decoders. Mac MPlayerX. MPlayer. Linux MPlayerFree. Image created in the YUV format, which splits color across Y, U, and V components; stores the brightness (luminance) as the Y value, and the color (chrominance) as U and V values; can be used for storing color information more accurately than the direct RGB representation. The YUV format is often written YUV. Windows Elecard YUV Viewer. ImageMagick. XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Mac MPlayerX. MPlayer. Linux MPlayer. Windows Elecard YUV Viewer. ImageMagick. XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".MIC",
    "Image Composer File",
    "2.2",
    "Web graphic created with Microsoft Image Composer, an image creation program that was packaged with FrontPage 98 and FrontPage 2000; may contain a simple graphic, banner, or animated image; saved as a small bitmap graphic ideal for Web publishing. Microsoft Image Composer was later replaced by Microsoft PhotoDraw. Both applications have been discontinued. Windows Microsoft Image Composer Microsoft PhotoDraw.",
    "Windows Microsoft Image Composer Microsoft PhotoDraw.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".ADC",
    "Scanstudio 16 Color Image",
    "2.2",
    "Four-bit color bitmap graphic created by ScanStudio, an algorithm that generates maps from laser range scans; stores geographical map information. ADC files are rarely used anymore. They can be opened by some older ESRI and SGSI GIS software products. Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. SGSI MapInfo Pro.",
    "Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. SGSI MapInfo Pro.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".Y",
    "Subsampled Raw YUV Image",
    "2.2",
    "Developer file used by Yacc (Yet Another Compiler-Compiler), a program used to generate source code parsers; contains formal declarations for how a programming language is defined; used for generating parsers for various languages. NOTE: Yacc has been used for creating the parser for the C programming language. Windows Microsoft Visual Studio with MKS Lex & Yacc plug-in. Any text editor Mac Apple Xcode. Berkeley Yacc. Yacc. Any text editor Linux Berkeley Yacc. Bison. Yacc. Any text editor. One of three files from a split.PPM file; others are.U and.V files; YUV representation is used by the Stanford MPEG codec. Windows Microsoft Windows Media Player with YUV Genius package Included with OS. Mac Apple QuickTime Player with QuickTime YUV codec Included with OS. A Y file is a compressed archive most likely created on an Amiga computer. It contains one or more files compressed using Yabba compression. While Yabba compression was used mostly on Amiga computers, a version of Yabba also existed for Unix. You can open a Y file with Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe (Windows, Mac) or Cloanto Amiga Forever (multiplatform). Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Cloanto Amiga Forever. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Cloanto Amiga Forever. Linux yabba for Unix Cloanto Amiga Forever.",
    "Windows Microsoft Visual Studio with MKS Lex & Yacc plug-in. Any text editor. Mac Apple Xcode. Berkeley Yacc. Yacc. Any text editor. Linux Berkeley Yacc. Bison. Yacc. Any text editor. Windows Microsoft Windows Media Player with YUV Genius package Included with OS. Mac Apple QuickTime Player with QuickTime YUV codec Included with OS. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Cloanto Amiga Forever. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Cloanto Amiga Forever. Linux yabba for Unix Cloanto Amiga Forever.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".CSF",
    "Content Sealed Format",
    "2.1",
    "A CSF file is a color management settings file used by Adobe Photoshop, InDesign, and Illustrator. It contains policies for color images, such as web graphic color definitions, ColorSync colors, prepress colors for different countries, and other color settings. CSF files are used for achieving color consistency between images and prints. NOTE: CSF files can be shared between Photoshop, InDesign, and Illustrator. They may also be managed using the Adobe Bridge application. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Coordinate system file used by GeoMedia, a GIS application used to analyze geographic information and produce maps; contains the coordinate system for an output data file that has no system in place; includes the base storage type, which is either Geographic, Projection, or Geocentric, of the coordinate system. A CSF file is used to define the coordinate system of input data with no specified coordinate system. It is created when the input data is exported to an output data format, such as the MicroStation V7 format. When it is exported, the CSF file is generated in the same location as the output file(s). NOTE: To create or edit a CSF file, use the Define Coordinate System File utility included with the GeoMedia software. ExportDGN.csf - The CSF file bear this name if multiple output files are produced. If only one output file is produced, the CSF file will be named with the same name as the output file. Windows Intergraph GeoMedia —  (Discontinued). Secure 2D image format that is a replica of the source image file; can embed print and watermark banners, limit printing and copying, and may include an expiration date; may also be password-protected; used for safe file sharing. Windows Informative Graphics Brava! Reader. 3D skeleton file created using Cal3D open source character animation software; stores a list of bones in the form of a parent to child relationship; used by the animation component for creating head, torso, leg, arm, and hand movements. Cal3D skeleton files can also be expressed in an XML form using.XSF files. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3DFree.",
    "Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Windows Intergraph GeoMedia —  (Discontinued). Windows Informative Graphics Brava! Reader. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3D.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".GVRS",
    "Gridfour Virtual Raster Store Image",
    "2.0",
    "A GVRS file is a grid-based raster image created by the Gridfour Virtual Raster Store, which is part of the Gridfour Software Project. Primarily, the Gridfour Virtual Raster Store is implemented as a Java API. This API compresses large raster images so applications can process them without overwhelming a devices memory. Projects such as Seabed 2030, which aims to map 100 percent of the ocean floor by the year 2030, produce a large amount of raster image-based data. To help applications process that data, developer Gary Lucas began work on the Gridfour Software Project. The Gridfour Software Projects primary goal is to optimize the compression, processing, and analysis of large raster image data sets. The Gridfour Software Project includes a module called the Gridfour Virtual Raster Store (GVRS). The GVRS API helps Java applications compress and manage raster image data that would typically be too large for a system to process. The API can save this compressed data in GVRS files, for future access and long-term archiving. Applications that use the Gridfour Virtual Raster Store (GVRS) Java API can open and process GVRS images. For more detailed information, refer to the Gridfour Virtual Raster Stores official documentation. Windows Gridfour Virtual Raster Store. Mac Gridfour Virtual Raster Store. Linux Gridfour Virtual Raster StoreFree.",
    "Windows Gridfour Virtual Raster Store. Mac Gridfour Virtual Raster Store. Linux Gridfour Virtual Raster Store.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".CPX",
    "Corel CMX Compressed File",
    "2.0",
    "A CPX file is a binding context file used by Oracle Application Development Framework (ADF) applications. It contains webpage tracking definitions as well as data bindings that map pages to data sources. CPX files are created when a data control is dropped onto a webpage using the JDeveloper HTML Visual Editor. CPX files are commonly found with the name DataBindings.xml. They are stored in an XML format. Windows Oracle JDeveloper Mac Oracle JDeveloper Linux Oracle JDeveloper. File used by Rise of Rome, an expansion pack for the Age of Empires game; contains a game campaign with missions and objectives; used to create and store custom game content. CPX files can be found in the campaign directory of an Age of Empires installation. Windows Microsoft Age of Empires: Rise of Rome. File used by Corel software for storing images; contains a compressed.CMX image file stored in a proprietary format; used for transferring images over the Internet or by email; can be opened and converted in CorelDRAW. Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023.",
    "Windows Oracle JDeveloper. Mac Oracle JDeveloper. Linux Oracle JDeveloper. Windows Microsoft Age of Empires: Rise of Rome. Windows CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".OIR",
    "FV3000 Specimen Image",
    "2.0",
    "An OIR file is an image created by an Olympus FV3000 laser scanning microscope. It contains a 2D or 3D image of a scientific specimen. The image may be a complete image of the specimen, or it may be a portion of a composite image. Scientists use the Olympus FV3000 to examine and create detailed, laser-scanned images of scientific specimens. For example, a biologist might use the FV3000 to image a portion of an animals brain. Images created using the FV3000 are saved as OIR files. Typically, each OIR file contains a complete image (which may be tiled to allow for detailed analysis). However, when creating an image larger than 1 GB, the FV3000 splits the image into multiple OIR files. To see the entirety of a split image, you must load all associated OIR files (e.g. for a split image that consists of two files, you must load both Example.oir and Example_00001.oir]). You can open an OIR file with OME Bio-Formats (multiplatform) or ImageJ (multiplatform). To open an OIR file with ImageJ, you must install the Olympus ImageJ plug-in. Windows OME Bio-Formats. ImageJ with Olympus ImageJ plug-in. Mac OME Bio-Formats. ImageJ with Olympus ImageJ plug-in. Linux OME Bio-Formats. ImageJ with Olympus ImageJ plug-inFree.",
    "Windows OME Bio-Formats. ImageJ with Olympus ImageJ plug-in. Mac OME Bio-Formats. ImageJ with Olympus ImageJ plug-in. Linux OME Bio-Formats. ImageJ with Olympus ImageJ plug-in.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".MIP",
    "Multiple Image Print File",
    "2.0",
    "Image file originally created for Paint Shop Pro, an image-editing program now known as PaintShop Photo Pro; contains multiple resolutions of the same.BMP image; often used for texture mapping purposes. MIP files allow users store graphics that are optimized for specific sizes. This way, images do not have to be stretched or compacted to fit. For example, a 512x512 pixel MIP image may also include a 32x32 pixel version for a thumbnail logo. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PALM",
    "Palm OS Bitmap Image",
    "2.0",
    "A PALM file is a bitmap image created by a Palm OS mobile device. It may contain a logo, clipart, photo, or other image meant to be shown in a Palm OS application. Different versions of Palm OS produce and use slightly different PALM files. PALM file open in ImageMagick Palm OS is a discontinued operating system that was used on Palm personal digital assistants (PDAs). The PALM file format is Palm OSs native image format. Many Palm OS application icons were stored as PALM files. Additionally, users could save images as PALM files in some programs. Versions 0 and 1 of the PALM file format did not support transparency or run-length encoding compression. Versions 2 and 3 did. NOTE: PALM files are also known as Palm Pilot Bitmap, Palm Pilot Tbmp, or Palm Pixmap images. You can open a PALM file with ImageMagick (multiplatform) or Netpbm (multiplatform). When opening a PALM file in ImageMagick, you may need to select All Files(*.*) to be able to select and open your PALM file. Web File Helper. Windows ImageMagick. Netpbm. Mac ImageMagick. Netpbm. Linux ImageMagick. NetpbmFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows ImageMagick. Netpbm. Mac ImageMagick. Netpbm. Linux ImageMagick. Netpbm.",
    "You can use ImageMagick to convert PALM files to the following image formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.WMF - Windows Metafile.MIFF - Magick Image.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics.EPS - Encapsulated PostScript.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".SIX",
    "Sixel Image",
    "2.0",
    "A SIX file is a raster image saved in the Sixel image format. It contains an image that was meant to be printed by a Digital Equipment Corporation (DEC) dot matrix printer or computer terminal. SIX files are comprised of sixels, which are sets of six pixel columns. SIX file open in ImageMagick DEC created the Sixel format for use on terminals and printers released in the 1980s. For example, the VT200 and VT300 series terminals can display images saved in the Sixel format. Each Sixel image, or SIX file, is comprised of binary data encoded into strings of six-bit numbers. Each number is then converted into an ASCII character. Programs that can read the Sixel format convert these ASCII character strings into raster images. SIX file open in File Viewer Plus 4 You can open a SIX file with ImageMagick (multiplatform) or SixelViewer (Windows). You can also view the text a SIX file contains in any text editor. Windows ImageMagick. SixelViewer. Any text editor Mac ImageMagick. Any text editor Linux ImageMagick. Any text editor.",
    "Windows ImageMagick. SixelViewer. Any text editor. Mac ImageMagick. Any text editor. Linux ImageMagick. Any text editor.",
    "You can use ImageMagick to convert SIX files to other image formats, including:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.WMF - Windows Metafile.MIFF - Magick Image.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics.EPS - Encapsulated PostScript.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PIC",
    "QuickTime PICT Image",
    "2.0",
    "Bitmap image created by IBM Lotus or a variety of other applications; possible programs include Advanced Art Studio, Micrografx Draw, and SoftImage 3D; should not be confused with the.PICT format. Web File Helper. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. XnViewMP. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree. Deep Raster image created by Houdini, a 3D modeling and animation application; stores a run-length encoded image, including the colors, color map, and size of the picture; supports any number of planes per pixel; stores images that can be included with 3D scenes. The PIC format is proprietary and is the native format used for internal Deep Raster images saved with Houdini. Windows SideFX Houdini. Mac SideFX Houdini. Linux SideFX Houdini. A PIC file is an image file saved in the PICtor raster image format. It is the native file format used by Pictor Paint (PC Paint) and Graphics Animation System for Professionals (GRASP), which were both developed by John Bridges for the MS-DOS operating system. PICtor PIC files are uncommon since the programs that support them are no longer developed. They were often used in the 1980s and 1990s to save and share images but are now rare. If you do encounter a PIC file, it most likely is an old image created by an MS-DOS paintbrush program. The image may also be a frame of a video sequence. The PICtor format is similar to the Paintbrush Bitmap Image.PCX format. It includes a header that contains information about the display device, which allows it to be viewed on different systems. After the header, the format stores image data that may be uncompressed or compressed with Run-length encoding (RLE)compression. You can open a PIC file with PMView Pro in Windows. You can also convert the PIC file to a more common format with FFmpeg and view it with an image viewer. Windows PMView Pro. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpegFree. Image generated by Apple QuickTime or the Apple QuickDraw API; contains a raster graphic stored in the.PICT format; used for storing image captures or other still frames. Windows XnViewMP. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. XnViewMP. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP. Windows SideFX Houdini. Mac SideFX Houdini. Linux SideFX Houdini. Windows PMView Pro. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg. Windows XnViewMP. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".LDOC",
    "CutOut Project",
    "2.0",
    "An LDOC file is a project created by FRANZIS CutOut, an app for cutting out objects in images. It stores an image with layers, masks, text, and other edits a CutOut user applies to a project. LDOC file open in FRANZIS CutOut 10 CutOut is a Windows app that provides various tools for removing images backgrounds and composing photo collages. In addition, the software allows you to save projects, close them, then re-open them for further editing. How to create an LDOC file To create an LDOC file with CutOut: Click the Menu icon Select File → Save as.. Choose Project file After you finish editing your project, you can save it in a widely supported image format, such as.JPEG or.TIFF. You can open an LDOC file with FRANZIS CutOut in Windows by clicking the Menu icon, then selecting Load project... Windows FRANZIS CutOut 10.",
    "Windows FRANZIS CutOut 10.",
    "CutOut can convert an LDOC file to the following image formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".NPSD",
    "NPS Image Editor Document",
    "2.0",
    "An NPSD file is an image file created by NPS Image Editor, a free, layer-based drawing and image editing program. It contains an image, as well as a record of the images layers and any edits made to the image. NPSD files can be opened only in NPS Image Editor. NPSD file open in NPS Image Editor NPS Image Editor is a lightweight pixel art, drawing, and photo editing application available for Windows. It allows users to create and save layer-based images as NPSD files, also known as NPS Image Editor Documents. Layer-based editing allows users to add and edit different image elements without interfering with other elements. For example, an NPS Image Editor user could add a text element on one image layer, add a shape element on a different image layer, and edit both entirely separately, without modifying the other. After a user has finished editing the image their NPSD file contains, they can use NPS Image Editor to export the image as a.JPG,.GIF,.PNG,.TIF, or.BMP image, for use in other image viewing and editing programs. Doing so will flatten the image, compressing all its layers into a single layer. You can open an NPSD file in NPS Image Editor (Windows). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your NPSD file. Windows NPS Image EditorFree.",
    "Windows NPS Image Editor.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".1SC",
    "Bio-Rad Quantity One Gel Image",
    "2.0",
    "A 1SC file is an image created by Bio-Rad Quantity One, a gel electrophoresis result analyzer. It contains a digital copy of a gel electrophoresis result. 1SC files are used to analyze results and share them with other Bio-Rad users. Biochemists use Bio-Rad gel imaging systems to record and analyze the results of gel electrophoresis tests. For example, a biochemist may use a Bio-Rad system to record and analyze the result of a western blot, which is a test that detects specific proteins in a tissue sample. Bio-Rad Quantity One is an analysis program that biochemists use to import, analyze, and save digital copies of their gel electrophoresis results. The images Quantity One creates are saved as 1SC files. You can open a 1SC file in Bio-Rad Quantity One (Windows). Those who do not have access to Bio-Rad Quantity One can use ImageJ and its accompanying Bio-Formats library (cross-platform) to view 1SC images. Windows Bio-Rad Quantity One ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Mac ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Linux ImageJ with Bio-Formats libraryFree.",
    "Windows Bio-Rad Quantity One ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Mac ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Linux ImageJ with Bio-Formats library.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PSDB",
    "PixelStyle Image",
    "2.0",
    "A PSDB file is an image created using Effectmatrix PixelStyle, a photo editor and vector graphic creation tool. It contains one or more image, text, drawing, and/or adjustment layers that, when viewed together, comprise a finalized image. You can use PixelStyle to export the image a PSDB file contains as a.JPG,.PNG,.JP2,.TIFF,.PDF,.BMP,.GIF, or.SVG file. PSDB file open in Effectmatrix PixelStyle 3 PixelStyles PSDB files are similar to Adobe Photoshops.PSD files. Like PSD files, PSDB files contain image elements separated into many layers. This allows photographers, graphic designers, and other users to adjust each image element separately, without affecting other parts of their image. How do I view a PSDB file outside of PixelStyle? If you want to view the image a PSDB file contains outside PixelStyle, you must export the image in a different file format. To export an image from PixelStyle, select File → Export.. from the programs menu bar. You can open a PSDB file in Effectmatrix PixelStyle (Mac). Note that while the free trial of PixelStyle allows you to open and create images, it does not allow you to save or export images. If you want to save or export PixelStyle images, you must purchase the program. Mac Effectmatrix PixelStyleFree.",
    "Mac Effectmatrix PixelStyle.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PSPTUBE",
    "PaintShop Pro Picture Tube File",
    "2.0",
    "A PSPTUBE file contains a picture tube created by PaintShop Pro, an image editor for Windows. It stores one or more graphics that you can dispense onto a canvas. PSPTUBE files also include settings, such as the cell arrangement and placement of the graphics that make up the paint tube. PSPTUBE file open in Corel PaintShop Pro 2023 PaintShop Pro is a raster image editor that provides various tools for creating images and editing digital photos. For example, one of its tools, the picture tube, allows you to add a repeating series of images to an image, such as a trail of dragonflies in a forest or a pattern of seashells on a beach. PaintShop Pro comes with pre-made picture tubes saved as PSPTUBE files in the following directory: C:/​ProgramData/​Corel/​Corel PaintShop Pro [version]/​Corel_10 Also, you can download more picture tube designs from Corels website or create your own by selecting File → Export → Picture Tube.. You can also select the Picture Tube Tool in the toolbar, select the Preset icon, then click the Save preset option. NOTE: For an image to be used as a picture tube, it must be 24-bit and only have one raster image with transparency. You can open a PSPTUBE file with Corel PaintShop Pro in Windows. You can select the Picture Tube Tool in the toolbar, select the Preset icon, and click the File Locations option. Then, click Add, navigate to the PSPTUBE file in the dialog, choose the PSPTUBE file, and click OK. You can also import a PSPTUBE file by placing it in the following directory: Documents/​Corel PaintShop Pro/​[version]/​Picture Tubes The picture tube should then be available in the Picture Tube Tool. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".VDOC",
    "VinylMaster Document",
    "2.0",
    "A VDOC file is an image created by VinylMaster, a sign-designing program. It contains an editable graphic intended to become a physical sign, decal, banner, or poster. VDOC files can be exported from VinylMaster as.EPS,.PDF, or.SVG files. VDOC file open in VinylMaster Cut 4 Future Corporation VinylMaster is a graphic design program that allows designers to mock up logos, signs, decals, banners, posters, and other marketing materials. Designers can then export their designs and provide them to printing companies, which use the designs to create physical marketing materials. By default, users VinylMaster designs are saved as VDOC files. This file format preserves the designs individual elements, allowing users to continue editing those elements in VinylMaster. However, VDOC files can be opened only in VinylMaster. When providing VinylMaster designs to print shops, designers typically export the designs as EPS, PDF, or SVG files, using VinylMasters File → Export.. option. That way, print shops can open and view the exported design, even if they dont have VinylMaster. You can open a VDOC file in VinylMaster (Windows). To do so, select File → Open.. from VinylMasters menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your VDOC file. You can open a VDOC file in any VinylMaster program, including VinylMaster Cut, Letter, Professional, Designer, and Expert. Windows Future Corporation VinylMaster.",
    "Windows Future Corporation VinylMaster.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PBS",
    "PixBuilder Studio Image",
    "2.0",
    "A PBS file is a presets file used by Corel PaintShop Pro, a program used for editing images and digital photos. It contains a collection of brush strokes used by the Brush tool in PaintShop Pro. PBS files include shape, texture, dynamics, and other data for each brush style. PaintShop Pro allows you to choose from different brush styles when using its brush tool on the canvas. The different presets for the brushes are stored in the PBS file and are used for simulating the texture of various types of brushes. Although you use the brush presets through the programs interface, you most likely will not come across an actual PBS file unless you download or receive new brushes from a site or another PaintShop Pro user. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. A PBS file is an image created by WnSoft PixBuilder Studio, a free image editing program for Windows. It contains one or more layers that comprise an image. PBS files can be exported from PixBuilder Studio as.BMP,.PNG,.JPG,.GIF,.TIFF,.PCX, and.TGA files. PBS file open in WnSoft PixBuilder Studio 2 PixBuilder Studio allows users to import and edit images using layer-based editing tools. For example, a user could import an image, adjust its color balance, add a new layer that contains text, and then save their edited image. If a user wants to preserve their edited images layers, they can save the image as a PBS file. This allows the user to reload their image and edit each layer individually at a later time. Alternatively, users can save images theyve edited in PixBuilder Studio as BMP, PNG, JPG, GIF, TIFF, PCX, or TGA files. However, saving an image in any of these formats flattens the image into a single layer. So, if a user saves their image in one of these file formats, they will not be able to continue editing the images layers. You can open a PBS file in PixBuilder Studio (Windows). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your PBS file. Windows WnSoft PixBuilder StudioFree.",
    "Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Windows WnSoft PixBuilder Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".VMU",
    "NanoZoomer Uncompressed Virtual Microscope Specimen",
    "2.0",
    "A VMU file is a whole slide image created by Hamamatsu NanoZoomer, a pathology slide scanning device. It is an archive that contains an index file and two or more.JPEG images. In contrast to.VMS files, VMU files are not compressed, so they are often quite large. Hamamatsu NanoZoomer is a high-speed, high-resolution digital slide scanner that pathologists use to create and examine digital images of pathology specimens. NanoZoomer saves slide specimen images in either the VMS, VMU, or.NDPI format. These formats are largely the same, except that VMS images are compressed and VMU images are not. VMU files are image archives that contain two or more JPEG images. One JPEG contains a high-resolution copy of a scanned slide. The other contains a lower-resolution copy. If the high-resolution image would be larger than 65,535 pixels on one side, NanoZoomer instead saves the image as multiple JPEGs. Slide-viewing software automatically combines these JPEGs into one slide image, using metadata saved in the archives index file. Windows users can open VMU files in OpenSlide, ImageJ, or NetScope Viewer. Mac and Linux users can open VMU files in OpenSlide or ImageJ. Mac OpenSlide. ImageJ. Windows OpenSlide. ImageJ. NetScope Viewer.",
    "Mac OpenSlide. ImageJ. Windows OpenSlide. ImageJ. NetScope Viewer.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".G3F",
    "Zetafax Fax Image",
    "2.0",
    "A G3F file is a fax image created by Zetafax fax software. It contains a copy of a faxed document, saved as a.TIFF image. Zetafax fax images may also be saved with the.G3N extension. Zetafax is a fax server software that allows businesses to fax documents to computers, fax machines, and other devices both within and outside their own network. When you fax or receive a document using Zetafax, the program saves a copy of the faxed document as a TIFF image. That image is stored within a G3F or G3N file. A G3F file contains a fine resolution (less compressed) copy of a faxed document, while a G3N file contains a normal resolution (more compressed) copy of the document. Zetafax creates either a G3F or G3N file to archive your faxed document, depending on whether you chose to fax or receive the document in fine or normal resolution. G3F and G3N files are stored in the directories you use to archive faxes sent and received using Zetafax. By default, these directories are C:/​Program Files/​Zetafax Server/​Server/​Z-Sent and C:/​Program Files/​Zetafax Server/​Server/​Z-Recd. You can open a G3F file (and view the faxed document it contains) in Zetafax Viewer, which is included with Zetafax (Windows). Alternatively, if you do not have access to Zetafax Viewer, you can rename your G3F file to use the.tiff extension and attempt to open it using any common image viewing application, such as Apple Preview (Mac), Microsoft Photos (Windows), or GIMP (cross-platform). Windows Equisys Zetafax. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. GIMP. Other image viewer Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. Other image viewer Linux GIMP. Other image viewer.",
    "Windows Equisys Zetafax. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. GIMP. Other image viewer. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. Other image viewer. Linux GIMP. Other image viewer.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".UPF",
    "Panono Unstitched Panorama Format",
    "2.0",
    "Settings file created by MicroStation, a 3D CAD modeling tool; saves user preferences such as hotkeys, workspace settings, and the settings specified in the Workspace → Preferences dialog; enables preferences to be remembered. Windows Bentley Systems MicroStation. A UPF file contains 36 images captured by Panono, a 360-degree panoramic camera. It stores 36 images that are captured by Panonos 36 cameras and saved in the Unstitched Panorama Format (UPF). The Panono is a spherical camera that is thrown into the air in order to capture 360-degree images from a unique angle. When the device is at its highest point, the 36 cameras on the device capture 36 images, which are stored in the UPF file. The images are unstitched, but when viewed in the Panono Cloud are stitched together for a seamless 360-degree image. You can download UPF files from the Panono Cloud and stitch the individual images stored in a UPF file together with third party software or convert the images to.JPEG format with the Panono UPF Converter. Windows Panono UPF Converter. Mac Panono UPF Converter. Linux Panono UPF Converter. Web Panono Cloud. CAD file created in the Unified Power Format (UPF), a format used for annotating an electrical power design; can save information for power sources, power controls, and protection mechanisms; enables a power design to be documented. The UPF standard was developed by Accellera but then given over to IEEE. Windows Accellera load_upf.",
    "Windows Bentley Systems MicroStation. Windows Panono UPF Converter. Mac Panono UPF Converter. Linux Panono UPF Converter. Web Panono Cloud. Windows Accellera load_upf.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".DC6",
    "Diablo II Graphics File",
    "2.0",
    "A DC6 file is a graphics file used by Diablo II, an action role-playing game released in 2000 by Blizzard Entertainment. It stores a graphic in DC6 format, which supports single and multi-frame images and is displayed during gameplay. DC6 files are used for animations and user interface (UI) elements, such as inventory items and background panels. Since Diablo II was released many years ago, DC6 files are uncommon. However, Diablo II gamers looking to modify gameplay will most likely encounter DC6 files when navigating the game resource files. While Blizzard Diablo II uses DC6 graphics for various aspects of gameplay and UI elements, you cannot open DC6 files directly with the game. If you are looking to modify DC6 files, you can convert them to the.PCX bitmap image format with DC6Con in Windows, then edit them with an application that supports PCX images, such as Adobe Photoshop or Corel Paintshop Pro. You can then convert the PCX files back to DC6 files with DC6Con or DC6 Creator. Windows Blizzard Diablo II. DC6ConFree.",
    "Windows Blizzard Diablo II. DC6Con.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".VIC",
    "VICAR Image",
    "2.0",
    "Contains import mappings used by ViziGen, a software development program for generating source code files for any programming language; controls how information from a UML modeling tool is imported into ViziGen. Windows ViziGen. Image created in the VICAR (Video Image Access and Retrieval) format, which was originally developed for planetary mission imaging data; contains an ASCII text header and one or more images saved as records of binary data; most commonly known for storing captured images from planetary mission systems. VICAR images were designed for the Jet Propulsion Laboratorys (JPL) unmanned planetary spacecraft. They were used during the 1970s and 1980s for the following missions: Mariner 9 to Mars, Mariner 10 to Mercury and Venus, Voyager to the outer planets. VICAR images are also used for cartography, biomedical, geology, and astronomy applications. Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. IMG2PNG XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows ViziGen. Windows Newera Graphics Converter Pro. IMG2PNG XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".XFACE",
    "X-Face Image",
    "2.0",
    "An XFACE file is an image saved in the X-Face file format. It contains a 48 x 48 pixel, black and white image. XFACE files were most often used as Usenet or email avatars. In the 1990s, email and Usenet users used XFACE files to embed a 48 x 48 pixel, black and white image within their emails and forum posts. These images served as users avatars. To add an X-Face image to an email or post, users added the X-Face: tag and encoded text to their message or posts header. For example, the following text could be used to add an X-Face avatar to an email: X-Face: jx]Pk3IoM&#)a#RB6p%|EHt9%2k^EzmZke#0mq+jf=/2QMp`-E3_Uk}^UiaOy^C,YFBvkw HT7O6wI;]fVKq~jN?1e[(_q8[`7c~L}[@nt|A,71:yiuLso5hmH*]e7AEy0OIdHgq-s${x]aw1Kh n+<]bzbXzYT!a&~Pk7p!u?hPN,8PqMBXgjeLa|Y/[cQ-L)X9+gVpX$/g1u^rq6Z)Sn$Yu%%jgMBNy $_TIDxI5[twnaVxZPZerB#a&5T1?_0j3C+Zl/#)q8&7Ebrp5J^N5;UXwCFzS<INQH21,~z%#y Actual XFACE files were created by Compface, an image compression utility developed by X-Face format creator James Ashton. These files stored the encoded text that users added to their email and forum post headers. NOTE: XFACE files are sometimes saved with the.FACE extension. Most popular image viewing applications cannot open XFACE files. However, you may be able to open an XFACE file using XNView MP (cross-platform) and convert it to a more usable image format using NConvert (cross-platform). If the file does not open natively, try renaming it to use the.face extension. Windows File Viewer Plus. XNViewMP. NConvert. Mac XNViewMP. NConvert. Linux XNViewMP. NConvertFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. XNViewMP. NConvert. Mac XNViewMP. NConvert. Linux XNViewMP. NConvert.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".WBD",
    "Webshots Picture File",
    "2.0",
    "Picture file used by Webshots Desktop Connect, a program used for sharing, organizing, and viewing pictures; contains a picture image stored in a proprietary format; used by Webshots to help users organize their pictures. NOTE: Webshots Desktop Connect was formerly known as Webshots Desktop and was owned by AG Interactive before being acquired by Threefold Photos in 2012. Mac XnViewMP. Ultimate Webshots Converter. Windows Threefold Photos Webshots Desktop Connect. Ultimate Webshots Converter. fCoder Group Image Converter Plus. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP. Ultimate Webshots ConverterFree.",
    "Mac XnViewMP. Ultimate Webshots Converter. Windows Threefold Photos Webshots Desktop Connect. Ultimate Webshots Converter. fCoder Group Image Converter Plus. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP. Ultimate Webshots Converter.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".COLZ",
    "Adobe Collage File",
    "2.0",
    "File created by Adobe Collage, an Adobe Touch App used for creating modern moodboards; may contain graphics and other content from.PDF,.PSD, and.AI files; can also include hand-drawn pen graphics and text; may be uploaded and shared on the Adobe Creative Cloud. COLZ files can be opened in Adobe Photoshop CS4 and later if the COLZ script is installed. Once installed, an option to import COLZ files is available from the File → Scripts → Import Adobe Collage menu option. Collage files can be uploaded and shared through Adobes Creative Cloud service. NOTE: Adobe Collage is no longer available as an Android app. Windows Adobe Photoshop with Adobe Collage COLZ script. Mac Adobe Photoshop with Adobe Collage COLZ script.",
    "Windows Adobe Photoshop with Adobe Collage COLZ script. Mac Adobe Photoshop with Adobe Collage COLZ script.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".NCT",
    "Nero CoverDesigner Template",
    "2.0",
    "File created by Now Contact, a contact information organizer; contains contact data such as a persons name, company, phone number, email, and address; also includes events connected to any contacts such as an appointment, phone call, or to-do task. To create the NCT file, select File → New.., select the Contact File icon, click OK, name the file, choose the save location, and click Save. To import another NCT file into your NCT file select File → Import.., navigate to the file, and select Open. You can synchronize your NCT file with another NCT file by selecting File → Synchronize → With a Now Contact File.., navigate to the NCT file, and click Sync. The NCT files must be of the same origin in order to synchronize with each other. Mac Now Contact. Windows Now ContactFree. CD or DVD artwork design template created by CoverDesigner, a disc label creator included with the Nero Multimedia Suite; contains the default layout, text, and graphics for a disc label; can be used as the basis for creating multiple.NCD files. Windows Nero 2022.",
    "Mac Now Contact. Windows Now Contact. Windows Nero 2022.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PSPFRAME",
    "PaintShop Pro Picture Frame File",
    "2.0",
    "A PSPFRAME file contains a picture frame created by PaintShop Pro, an image editor for Windows. It stores a picture frame graphic that you can apply to an image. PSPFRAME graphics come in various styles, including oval, modern, and classic, with mats or photo edges. PSPFRAME file open in Corel PaintShop Pro 2023 PaintShop Pro is a raster image editor that comes with various tools to create graphics and edit digital photos, including camera raw images. The picture frame tool allows you to add a digital frame around an image to direct the focus of the viewers perspective. PaintShop Pro comes with pre-made picture frames saved as PSPFRAME files in the following directory: C:/​ProgramData/​Corel/​Corel PaintShop Pro [version]/​Corel_09 You can also create custom picture frames and save them as PSPFRAME files by selecting File → Save As... You can open a PSPFRAME file with Corel PaintShop Pro in Windows. To add a picture frame to an image of a PSPFRAME file, select Image → Picture Frame.. You can also import a PSPFRAME file by placing it in the following directory: Documents/​Corel PaintShop Pro/​[version]/​Picture Frames The picture frame will then be available in the Picture Frame Tool. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".DM3",
    "DigitalMicrograph Image",
    "2.0",
    "Raster image created by DigitalMicrograph, a application used for viewing and analyzing captured microscope images; stores the image and includes metadata such as the microscopes CCD camera properties, the exposure length, and a timestamp; uses a proprietary format. Mac ImageJ with DM3_Reader plug-in. Windows Gatan DigitalMicrograph. ImageJ with DM3_Reader plug-in. Linux ImageJ with DM3_Reader plug-inFree. A DM3 file is a gameplay recording created by id Software Quake III Arena. It contains footage a player recorded while playing Quake III. xsDM3 files are commonly referred to as Quake III demos. Id Software released Quake III Arena in late 1999. This entry in the popular Quake series focused on online, multiplayer gameplay. To allow players to review and study previous matches, Quake III included a recording function that players could use to record their gameplay. To begin recording, players entered the /record console command. To stop recording, they entered /stoprecord. In versions 1.11 to 1.17, Quake III saved the recordings players created as DM3 files. Players could review and play the DM3 files theyd created using Quake IIIs Demos menu. They could also use the /demo console command to play a specific DM3 file. NOTE: Later versions of Quake III save demos as.dm_48,.dm_66,.dm_67, and.DM_68 files. In Quake III Arena (multiplatform), you can play DM3 files from the Demos menu or using the /demo console command. Outside Quake III, you can use wolfcamql (multiplatform), Seismovision (Windows), or Uber Demo Tools (multiplatform) to play the demo a DM3 file contains. Mac id Software Quake 3. wolfcamql. Uber Demo Tools. Windows id Software Quake 3. wolfcamql. Uber Demo Tools. Seismovision. Linux id Software Quake 3. wolfcamql. Uber Demo ToolsFree. A DM3 file is a disk information file created by Diskette Manager 3, an MS-DOS disk cataloging program. It specifies a disks name, description, file list, and related metadata. Diskette Manager 3 places a DM3 file on each disk you catalog using the program. Diskette Manager 3 is a program that allows users to catalog all their diskettes and floppy disks, as well as those disks contents, in a single database. The program also allows users to print adhesive labels that detail each cataloged disks contents. Users can apply these labels to their disks to make searching for a specific disk easier. When a user catalogs a disk using Diskette Manager 3, the program places a DM3 file on that disk. Each disks DM3 file includes all that disks cataloged information, including the disks name, contents, comments, date cataloged, type, and bytes used. Because DM3 files are plain text files, you can open and edit them in any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or GitHub Atom (multiplatform). Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor Windows Bloc Publishing Diskette Manager 3 Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor Linux GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor.",
    "Mac ImageJ with DM3_Reader plug-in. Windows Gatan DigitalMicrograph. ImageJ with DM3_Reader plug-in. Linux ImageJ with DM3_Reader plug-in. Mac id Software Quake 3. wolfcamql. Uber Demo Tools. Windows id Software Quake 3. wolfcamql. Uber Demo Tools. Seismovision. Linux id Software Quake 3. wolfcamql. Uber Demo Tools. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Windows Bloc Publishing Diskette Manager 3 Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Linux GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".T2K",
    "Canfield Image File",
    "2.0",
    "Test document created by Teach2000, a memory training application; saves a list of questions and answers in an XML format; may include free form or multiple choice questions. T2K files are used for saving memorization questions and can be run as a test in Teach2000. They can also be used by teachers for creating.T2KT files, which are distributed as digital tests for students. Windows Basement.nl Teach2000Free. A T2K file is an image saved in the Canfield Image format, which is used to store images of patients for medical imaging purposes. It contains image data captured by a Canfield Scientific device, such as a TwinFlash RL Clinical Camera or IntelliStudio photography system. T2K image files can be opened with Canfield Scientific Mirror medical imaging software. You will most likely only encounter a T2K image file if you are a medical professional in the plastic surgery field. The images are typically created in the consultation phase of a visit with a plastic surgeon using a Canfield Scientific device. Then, the professional transfers the files to a computer running Windows and imports them into Mirror software to be analyzed and displayed for the patient to see. The images are used to consult patients for a variety of procedures, such as facelifts, necklifts, rhinoplasty, and liposuction. A T2K file may be accidentally shared with a patient who does not have access to Mirror software. Unfortunately, there is no program besides Mirror software that supports the encrypted T2K image format. The patient would have to contact the medical professional and have him export the image in Mirror in JPEG format, which is supported by many image viewers. Windows Canfield Scientific Mirror Suite. Canfield Scientific PhotoFile.",
    "Windows Basement.nl Teach2000. Windows Canfield Scientific Mirror Suite. Canfield Scientific PhotoFile.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".TRIF",
    "Tiled Raster Interchange Format",
    "2.0",
    "Bitmap image file created in the TRIF format, which was designed by the Tiling Task Group (TTG) and sponsored by the National Bureau of Standards in 1987; supports bitonal images that are tiled with fixed-size squares. TRIF files are used for exchanging large engineering drawings in a black and white raster format. Windows Open with program that created original file.",
    "Windows Open with program that created original file.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".BRN",
    "Cube Graphics File",
    "2.0",
    "File created by BrainStorm, a program used for capturing ideas in a structured manner; contains a title for an idea and subpoints, which together comprise a tree of information; may store references to files, pictures, hyperlinks, and other information; can be viewed from different perspectives in the software. BrainStorm BRN files can be published to HTML for sharing on the Web. Windows BrainStormFree. Graphics file used by HTC Touch mobile phones for displaying Cube animations; saves a collection of bitmap images that are read by the phone to display the 3D cube animation; can be converted between the.BMP and BRN format using BRN Converter; sometimes replaced by custom graphics for use on the phone. Windows Brn ConverterFree. Game data file used by Gabriel Knight 3: Blood of the Sacred, Blood of the Damned, an adventure game released in 1999; referred to as a barn file because it houses various kinds of data for the game; can be extracted to the enclosed source files using GK3 Barn Browser. Windows GK3 Barn Browser. Sierra Entertainment Gabriel Knight 3.",
    "Windows BrainStorm. Windows Brn Converter. Windows GK3 Barn Browser. Sierra Entertainment Gabriel Knight 3.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".JAS",
    "Paint Shop Pro Compressed Graphic",
    "2.0",
    "3D model file created by Cheetah3D, a 3D modeling, rendering, and animation program for Mac; contains three-dimensional objects, visual effects, and animation properties; often used for digital art. Unity can import and modify JAS files, as well as convert JAS files to the Autodesk.FBX format. Windows Unity Technologies Unity. Mac Cheetah3D. Unity Technologies Unity. Linux Unity Technologies UnityFree. 24-bit color or 8-bit grayscale image compressed by Jasc Paint Shop Pro. NOTE: Corel acquired Jasc Software in October, 2004. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "Windows Unity Technologies Unity. Mac Cheetah3D. Unity Technologies Unity. Linux Unity Technologies Unity. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PC3",
    "Degas Elite High Res Image File",
    "2.0",
    "File created by AutoCAD, a CAD program used to create 2D and 3D designs; contains plotter properties, such as color depth, media type, and print quality; used to configure specific plotter settings and save them for later use. PC3 files commonly have corresponding.PMP files, which provide additional plotter calibration information. To create a PC3 file in AutoCAD, select File → Plotter Manager → Add-a-Plotter Wizard. NOTE: PC3 files apply to the AutoCAD 2000 and later. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Image format used by Degas Elite, an image editor for the Atari ST platform; supports 2 colors and an image resolution of 640x400 pixels; can be opened directly on Atari systems using Degas Elite software. Degas Elite 3 files also use the.PI3 file extension. Windows XnViewMP. Mac Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Windows XnViewMP. Mac Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PE4",
    "PhotoImpact Image Archive",
    "2.0",
    "Archive or cache of thumbnail images used by Ulead Photo Explorer; contains small versions of images stored in a photo album; makes it possible to quickly browse through the images in an album. Windows Ulead Photo Explorer. Archive of thumbnail images saved by PhotoImpact 4.x; contains small images that represent the larger image files stored in a photo album. PE4 files were originally used by Photo Explorer. Windows Ulead PhotoImpact —  (Discontinued). Trial.",
    "Windows Ulead Photo Explorer. Windows Ulead PhotoImpact —  (Discontinued). Trial.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".FAX",
    "Fax Document",
    "2.0",
    "Fax template created by Now Contact, a program that organizes contact information and day-to-day activities; contains a print layout template for your fax document; pre-loaded options include Fancy Fax, Flower, Simple Cover, and Swoosh.. To create the FAX file, select Define → Print Templates → Faxes.., select the + button in the top-right, name the template, and click OK. You will then be able to edit the template layout and its dimensions. Click OK when youre finished. When creating a new.NWP fax document, you can select a FAX template to work off of by choosing a template from the Use Template drop-down menu. To select the template you want to print from, select File → Print Templates.., choose your template from the Template Type drop-down menu, and click OK. Windows Now Contact. Mac Now ContactFree. A FAX file is an image of a fax created or received with fax software, including the GFI FaxMaker faxing service. It is saved in a TIFF format, which most image viewing and editing applications recognize. Typically, fax software creates a FAX file from a scanned document, receipt, etc., then sends it to a user in another location using compatible fax software to view the image of the scanned material. In the 1980s, 1990s, and 2000s, fax machines were commonplace in office environments. The devices allowed you to scan printed material, such as a financial paper document, as a bitmap image, then send it to a telephone number connected to a printer to print the scanned material. Some fax software offerings, like the aforementioned GFI FaxMaker app, save the scanned material as FAX files, which are renamed.TIF files. By saving the scans as FAX files, you could archive them or send them at a later time. You can open a FAX file with any image viewer or editor that supports the TIFF format. Options include Microsoft Photos (bundled with Windows) and Apple Preview (bundled with macOS). You may need to rename the.fax file extension to the.tif file extension for image viewers and editors to recognize and open the FAX file. Windows Microsoft Windows. Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Apple Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer Linux GIMPFree.",
    "Windows Now Contact. Mac Now Contact. Windows Microsoft Windows. Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Apple Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer. Linux GIMP.",
    "Since FAX files are saved in a TIFF format, many image viewers and editors, including Microsoft Photos, Apple Preview, and Adobe Photoshop, can convert FAX files to other image formats. For example, Microsoft Photos can convert FAX files to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.BMP - Bitmap Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image NOTE: You may need to rename the.fax file extension to the.tif file extension for image viewers and editors to recognize and open the FAX file."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".ICPR",
    "IconUtils Project File",
    "2.0",
    "Project file created by IconUtils, a software package used to create and edit Windows icons (.ICO); saves edited graphics for an icon, icon library, cursor, or cursor library; used for saving icons and cursors that can be used for styling the look and feel of the Windows environment. When editing is complete, you can export IconUtils projects to icon files, cursor files (.CUR,.ANI), icon library files (.ICL), or cursor library files (.CL). They can also be exported to several standard bitmap graphic formats. NOTE: ICPR files are actually saved by IconLover, a program included with the IconUtils software package. Other Aha-Soft applications can also save ICPR files, including ArtIcons Pro. Windows Aha-Soft IconUtils. Aha-Soft ArtIcons Pro.",
    "Windows Aha-Soft IconUtils. Aha-Soft ArtIcons Pro.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PTX",
    "V.Flash PTX Image",
    "2.0",
    "Session file format introduced with Pro Tools 10 digital audio workstation (DAW) software; supports audio, MIDI, and software instrument tracks, as well as effects, mixing settings, and other edits; stores references to audio files but not the audio files themselves. NOTE: Pro Tools 7-9 use the.PTF format and cannot open PTX files. But, you can convert PTX files to the PTF format with Pro Tools 10 and later in the Save Session Copy dialog. Note that some newer Pro Tools 10 features will be lost if you save to the older format, such as clip gain settings. Windows Avid Pro Tools. Mac Avid Pro Tools. File created by E-Transcript Manager, a program used for creating certified electronic transcripts; contains transcript data recorded from a courtroom hearing; most commonly used by court reporting firms when creating legal transcripts for attorneys; created to reduce the file size of emailed transcripts. E-Transcripts may also use the .exe extension, which allows the transcript to be viewed from a self-contained file. However, email filters often stop the delivery of .exe files. For this reason, the PTX file format was created as non-executable format to more easily bypass email server filters. PTX E-Transcripts may be converted back and forth between .exe E-Transcripts. NOTE: RealLegal, the developers of the PTX format, were acquired by LiveNote and then by Thomson West. Both the West and RealLegal brands are used to advertise and sell similar software applications. The Mac version of RealLegal E-Transcript Viewer is only available for Mac OS Classic, the predecessor to Mac OS X. Windows West RealLegal E-Transcript Viewer. West E-Transcript Bundle Viewer. West RealLegal E-Transcript Manager. West Publisher —  (Discontinued). West RealLegal E-Transcript Reporter Edition. Mac West RealLegal E-Transcript ViewerFree. Uncompressed RAW image file captured with a Pentax camera; saves image data exactly as recorded by the cameras sensor; can be viewed using the Pentax software included with the camera. Most Pentax RAW image files use the.PEF extension. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Pentax Photo Browser or Photo Laboratory MAGIX Xara Xtreme UFRaw. Mac Pentax Photo Browser or Photo UFRaw. MacPhun ColorStrokes. Linux UFRaw (Unidentified Flying Raw) The GIMP with UFRaw plugin. A PTX file is an image saved in the V.Flash PTX raster image format. It is used to store graphics for games for the V.Flash educational gaming console released in 2006. The V.Flash PTX format consists of a header followed by the image data. PTX files are uncommon since they are only used in games that have been discontinued. The VTech V.Flash gaming console was discontinued in 2007, a year after it was released. You most likely will only encounter a PTX file if you dump the game files from the CD in which the game is delivered. The Amazing Spider-Man: Countdown To Doom video game for the VTech V.Flash gaming console. NOTE: Some games that use the V.Flash PTX format include The Amazing Spider-Man: Countdown to Doom, Cars: In the Fast Lane, and SpongeBob SquarePants: Idea Sponge. Since the PTX format is rare, there are few programs that support it. However, you can upload a PTX file to Toms Editor, which is an online application, to view or convert the image. If you are looking to just convert a PTX file to a more common image format, you can use FFmpeg. After converting the PTX file, you can open it with an image editor. Windows File Viewer Plus. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg. Web Toms EditorFree. Texture preset file used by Paint Shop Pro, an image editing program; stores image texture information used for applying textures to shapes and objects within Paint Shop Pro; often saved along with a corresponding.BMP file. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. A PTX file is an image file used in a PopCap Games video game, such as Plants vs. Zombies 2. It contains an image used as an in-game background, item, or character. In Plants vs. Zombies games, PTX files are stored in the main.pak/​images directory. PTX files may be compressed or uncompressed. In Android versions of Plants vs. Zombies games, compressed PTX files are compressed using Ericsson Texture Compression (ETC1). In iOS versions of Plants vs. Zombies games, compressed PTX files are compressed using PowerVR Texture Compression (PVRTC). You can use the Taiji Plants vs. Zombies 2 hacking tool to convert PTX images to.PNG images. Then, you can open the converted images in any image viewing application. Windows Plants vs. Zombies 2 Hacking Tools. iOS PopCap Games Plants Vs. Zombies 2. Android PopCap Games Plants Vs. Zombies 2.",
    "Windows Avid Pro Tools. Mac Avid Pro Tools. Windows West RealLegal E-Transcript Viewer. West E-Transcript Bundle Viewer. West RealLegal E-Transcript Manager. West Publisher —  (Discontinued). West RealLegal E-Transcript Reporter Edition. Mac West RealLegal E-Transcript Viewer. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Pentax Photo Browser or Photo Laboratory MAGIX Xara Xtreme UFRaw. Mac Pentax Photo Browser or Photo UFRaw. MacPhun ColorStrokes. Linux UFRaw (Unidentified Flying Raw) The GIMP with UFRaw plugin. Windows File Viewer Plus. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg. Web Toms Editor. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Windows Plants vs. Zombies 2 Hacking Tools. iOS PopCap Games Plants Vs. Zombies 2. Android PopCap Games Plants Vs. Zombies 2.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".DC2",
    "Kodak Photo-Enhancer File",
    "2.0",
    "2D drawing created by DesignCAD, a CAD design and drafting application; encodes the drawing in ASCII text and includes all drawn elements; used as a plain text alternative to the.DCD drawing format. Windows IMSI DesignCAD. IMSI DesignCAD 3D Max. Camera RAW file created by some Kodak digital cameras; stores the image in an uncompressed format exactly as it was captured on the camera; often imported into photo-editing software for touch-ups and publishing. Windows FileStream Image Broadway. Adobe Photoshop with LaserSoft Imaging SilverFast DC plug-in. Mac Adobe Photoshop with LaserSoft Imaging SilverFast DC plug-in. CAD document created by DevCad Cam Professional, a program used for creating CAD designs; supports all of the features of DevCad Pro.DC1 files but also can store CNC milling machine instructions for automated milling. DevCad Cam Pro can visually simulate the toolpaths stored in DC2 files. Windows DevCad Cam Pro.",
    "Windows IMSI DesignCAD. IMSI DesignCAD 3D Max. Windows FileStream Image Broadway. Adobe Photoshop with LaserSoft Imaging SilverFast DC plug-in. Mac Adobe Photoshop with LaserSoft Imaging SilverFast DC plug-in. Windows DevCad Cam Pro.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PFR",
    "Paint Shop Pro Picture Frame File",
    "2.0",
    "Compact, platform-independent format for representing high-quality, scalable outline fonts; based on the TrueDoc PFR Specification developed by Bitstream, Inc; used for embedding rasterized fonts into Web pages and for displaying text on digital televisions. The PFR font format is used by several organizations that set digital TV standards. These organizations include ATDC, DAVIC, DVB, DTG, MHP, and OCAP. Windows Bitstream Font Fusion or TrueDoc. Image used by Paint Shop Pro, a graphics editor now known as PaintShop Photo Pro; stores a custom or preset picture frame graphic; can be used as a border for one or more images. NOTE: PFR files are not supported by the newer PaintShop Photo Pro. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "Windows Bitstream Font Fusion or TrueDoc. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PXICON",
    "CandyBar Icon",
    "2.0",
    "Icon image used by CandyBar, a program used for customizing icons in the Mac OS X environment; saves multiple images in a single file, each with different resolutions representing the standard icon sizes (i.e., 512x512, 256x256, 128x128, etc.). Many different PXICON files are included with the CandyBar installation in the ~/​Library/​Application Support/​CandyBar/​Icons/​ directory. NOTE: PX stands for Pixadex, the software from The Iconfactory that was merged into the CandyBar application. Pixadex icons use the.PIXADEX extension. Mac Panic CandyBar —  (Discontinued).",
    "Mac Panic CandyBar —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".ACR",
    "American College of Radiology File",
    "2.0",
    "Script created with ACRobot (AutoCursorRobot), a program that creates scripts for mouse and keyboard actions; used for automating common tasks and speeding up repetitive jobs. ACR files are created using ACRobots built-in scripting language. However, they are recorded based on the users actions and do not require any manual programming. Windows Acr-Soft ACRobot. File generated by Image Comparer, a program used for identifying duplicate audio files on the hard drive; saves the results of comparing audio files (i.e., songs and music) with each other; enables users to review the comparisons later without having to re-process them again. Windows Bolide Audio Comparer. Full system backup created with Acers eRecovery Management tool, a backup utility included with Acer computers; contains the entire contents of a hard disk, including both the system and user files. ACR files can be burned to a CD or DVD and can be used to restore an entire system using the eRecovery Management program. Windows Acer eRecovery Management. Medical image file format used by the National Electrical Manufacturers Association (ACR-NEMA); stores an image taken by radiological equipment; used to store patient records in a digital format. The.DCM file format is more commonly used to store radiological images. Windows AMIDE XnViewMP. Mac AMIDE XnViewMP. Linux AMIDE XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows Acr-Soft ACRobot. Windows Bolide Audio Comparer. Windows Acer eRecovery Management. Windows AMIDE XnViewMP. Mac AMIDE XnViewMP. Linux AMIDE XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".THM",
    "GoPro Thumbnail Image",
    "2.0",
    "A THM file is a theme file used by Sony Ericsson mobile phones. It stores settings used to customize the user interface of the cell phone and includes custom window and text colors, icons, wallpaper, and other images. THM files can be created and edited using the free Themes Creator from Sony Ericsson, which is no longer developed. Windows Sony Ericsson Themes Creator Mac Sony Ericsson Themes Creator. A THM file is a thumbnail image generated by digital camcorders and software programs when saving a video clip. It contains a small image from the video clips first frame and is displayed to help a user identify a clip when visually browsing through a collection of video clips. THM files often are saved in the JPEG format. When you are capturing video with a digital camcorder or camera, the device creates a thumbnail of the video and saves it to its memory card or internal storage. Then, when you import video from a camcorder or camera, the software you are using to transfer the video also transfers the associated THM files. Each THM file transferred from a device to a computer shares the same filename as its associated video clip. For example, a THM file for clip001.avi is created as clip001.thm. You will likely never need to open a THM file since the software program you use to browse video clips displays the thumbnail image next to the video clip. However, if you encounter a THM file and need to open it individually, you can attempt to open it directly with an image viewer, such as Microsoft Photos, Microsoft Paint, or Apple Preview. If that does not work, you can change the.thm file extension to.jpg and attempt again to open it with an image viewer. NOTE: If the THM file is not saved in JPEG format, you will likely be unable to open it with an image editor. Windows Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. Microsoft Paint Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Sony Picture Motion Browser —  (Discontinued). Other image viewer Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer Linux Any image viewer. Macro file used by Thermwood CNC Routers; contains router machining instructions that automate router processes; a list of CNC events are also saved in a file named hist.thm.. Windows Thermwood Mastercam. A THM file is a thumbnail image, which is a small, icon-sized image that represents a larger image. It is saved in a bitmap format similar to a.JPG file but at a lower resolution. Digital camera and photo or video-editing apps often create THM files to store small previews of larger images and videos. THM file open in Apple Preview 11 The purpose of THM thumbnails is to provide a quick preview that gives you an idea of the image, video, clip art, etc., you are browsing. Since the thumbnail is saved at such a low resolution, it is not meant to be opened and viewed the same as the original file for which it stores the preview. You can open THM files with various image viewers and editors, such as Microsoft Photos (Windows) and Apple Preview (Mac). For example, to open a THM file with Preview, select File → Open. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. A THM file is a raster image saved in the GoPro Thumbnail format. It stores image data similar to the JPEG format but also contains GoPro-specific metadata, including the date and time it was captured and the settings of the camera. GoPro cameras, such as the HERO2 and HERO3, automatically generate THM thumbnail images from captured footage to help users preview images and video. Select GoPro cameras create THM and.LRV files to accompany captured footage to aid you as you browse through your footage on the camera screen or your mobile phone (using the Quik app). For example, a GoPro HERO2 user will find a THM and LRV file next to their.MP4 video. The THM file is a small preview (typically 160x120) created from a single frame in your footage that is also small in size to allow for quicker loading times as you scroll. Additionally, the LRV file is a low-resolution video utilized during the editing process to reduce the amount of computing power required to edit a video. Deleting GoPro THM files You can delete THM files to remove clutter, but it may affect the speed at which you can preview footage on the camera or in the Quik app. However, the actual footage will not be affected. GOPR0[numbered video].THM - GoPro cameras name the THM file after the MP4 file it accompanies. For example, if you just recorded the 120th video, GoPro names the MP4 video GOPR0120.MP4 and the thumbnail GOPR0120.THM. THM files are not meant to be manually opened. Instead, GoPro cameras and the Quik app (iOS and Android) reference them for quicker loading times as you browse through footage. However, since the files are saved in a JPEG format, you may be able to view them with an app that supports JPEG images. iOS GoPro Quik. Android GoPro Quik.",
    "Windows Sony Ericsson Themes Creator. Mac Sony Ericsson Themes Creator. Windows Microsoft Windows Photo Viewer Included with OS. Microsoft Paint Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Sony Picture Motion Browser —  (Discontinued). Other image viewer. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Other image viewer. Linux Any image viewer. Windows Thermwood Mastercam. Windows Microsoft Photos Included with OS. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. iOS GoPro Quik. Android GoPro Quik.",
    "If the THM file is saved in JPEG format, you can convert it to other formats with many image editors, including Microsoft Paint, Adobe Photoshop, and Apple Preview. For example, Paint can convert THM files saved in JPEG format to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.JFIF - JPEG File Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.HEIC - High Efficiency Image Format.DIB - Device Independent Bitmap. Apple Preview and Microsoft Photos can convert THM files to other formats. For example, Preview can convert THM files to the following formats:.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.EXR - OpenEXR Image.HEIC - High Efficiency Image Format.PDF - Portable Document Format."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".SUNIFF",
    "Sun TAAC IFF Image",
    "2.0",
    "A SUNIFF file is a raster image saved in the Sun TAAC Image File Format (SUNIFF). It contains a paletted, full RGB or RGBA image. SUNIFF files are uncompressed. Sun Microsystems developed the SUNIFF format for use on its proprietary workstations. SUNIFF files may instead be saved with the.TAAC or.VFF extensions. You can open a SUNIFF file with XnViewMP (multiplatform). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your file. Windows XnViewMP. Logipole Konvertor. Mac XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows XnViewMP. Logipole Konvertor. Mac XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "You can use Logipole Konvertor (Windows) or XnViewMP (multiplatform) to convert SUNIFF files to other image formats. For example, XnViewMP can convert SUNIFF files to the following formats (and many others):.JPG - JPEG Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.JP2 - JPEG 2000 Core Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image.WEBP - WebP Image."],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".RIC",
    "NXT Image File",
    "2.0",
    "Image format used for displaying images on the LEGO Mindstorms NXT brick, the brain of an NXT robot; may include multiple sprite sheets, CopyBits, VarMaps, parameters, and other data. By default, the NXT-G programming environment displays the first sprite sheet in a program. Display parameters can be modified using.NXC program files. NOTE: LEGO MINDSTORMS NXT evolved into LEGO MINDSTORMS EV3 in 2013. Windows National Instruments LabVIEW For LEGO Mindstorms —  (Discontinued). Trial nxtRICedit nxtRICeditV2 NXT-G.",
    "Windows National Instruments LabVIEW For LEGO Mindstorms —  (Discontinued). Trial nxtRICedit nxtRICeditV2 NXT-G.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".PAL",
    "Dr. Halo Color Palette File",
    "2.0",
    "Settings file created by Corel Painter, a digital art application; saves the layout of workspace palettes, such as the Mixer, Layers, Color, and Navigator palettes; allows artists to customize screen layouts for different painting needs. Custom palettes can be saved by selecting Window → Arrange Palettes → Save Layout.. They can be loaded by selecting Window → Arrange Palettes and then choosing a custom palette from the menu. The default arrangement is called Default. NOTE: PAL files are not manually saved by the user. Instead Corel Painter uses PAL files to allow the user to load and save palette arrangements through the user interface. Windows Corel Painter 2022. Mac Corel Painter 2022. A PAL file contains a color palette used by various Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) emulators. It stores information about the intensity of red, green, and blue colors for the output of emulated games. PAL files are used to emulate the PPU of the NES, which is a chip that outputs RGB video from the system to the screen. The PAL file typically stores 64 3-byte RGB entries since there are 64 NES color values. Windows Nestopia. Mac Nestopia. Linux NestopiaFree. A PAL file contains one or more 3D objects used by PhotoAnim, a free Windows program used to edit and animate images. It stores 3D objects that can be inserted into a scene, such as shapes, vehicles, trees, people, or furniture. To open a PAL file in PhotoAnim, select File → Load Object.. To create a PAL file in PhotoAnim, select File → Save As Object... Windows PhotoAnimFree. Palette of colors used by Dr. Halo bitmap images (.CUT files); specifies the maximum allowable red, green, and blue color values; also contains the color palette, which stores RGB values on a 0-255 scale; used to alter an images colors without having to re-encode the CUT image. Windows Dr. Halo III Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows Corel Painter 2022. Mac Corel Painter 2022. Windows Nestopia. Mac Nestopia. Linux Nestopia. Windows PhotoAnim. Windows Dr. Halo III Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["raster_image_files",
    ".SID",
    "ScanIt Document",
    "2.0",
    "Backup file created by Steam, an application used to download and manage Valve video games on desktop computers; contains compressed game data created by the Steam backup feature (steambackup.exe program); used to backup games to DVDs or other external media. SID files are created with a.SIS file and a.SIM file, which provide metadata necessary to restore backup game data. SID files use the naming convention {game}_disk{X}_{Y}.sid, where game is the name of the backup game, X is the disk number, and Y is the backup file number on the disk. NOTE: Steam backups do not include saved games, custom multiplayer maps, or configuration files. You must backup and restore those files manually. Windows Valve Steam. Mac Valve Steam. Image created using Multi-resolution Seamless Image Database (MrSID) compression, which was developed by Extensis for compressing large images; commonly used to partition and store large Geographic Information Systems (GIS) images. NOTE: Extensis was formerly known as LizardTech. Windows Extensis GeoExpress. Extensis GeoViewer. Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. ERDAS IMAGINE. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in Mac Extensis SquishPic. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in Linux Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. Audio file originally used by Commodore computer systems, but now more often used for playing the sounds on Commodore emulators and SID software players; often used for video game background music and can use mono or stereo audio formats; created for the MOS Technology 6502 processor, which can be emulated by newer desktop software to play the audio. SID files may use the PSID format or the newer RSID (Real SID) format. While the PSID format is more compatible with general Commodore emulation software, the RSID format requires more complete emulation of the C64 hardware. Windows ACID 64 Player. quadraSID. Mac SIDPLAY. quadraSID. Linux Audacious. SIDPlayerFree. Document created and used by ScanIt, an application used to extract data from graphs; contains the graph image and its metadata; includes axes definitions, document windows, and other document specific options. The SID file allows you to save your progress and continue it at a later time. The file can be saved to a variety of image formats, such as.JPEG,.PNG,.TIF, and.BMP. Windows AmsterCHEM ScanItFree.",
    "Windows Valve Steam. Mac Valve Steam. Windows Extensis GeoExpress. Extensis GeoViewer. Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. ERDAS IMAGINE. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in. Mac Extensis SquishPic. A Web browser with LizardTech ExpressView (MrSID) Browser Plug-in. Linux Extensis Express Server. Extensis SquishPic. Windows ACID 64 Player. quadraSID. Mac SIDPLAY. quadraSID. Linux Audacious. SIDPlayer. Windows AmsterCHEM ScanIt.",
    "?"],
