    ["raster_image_files",
    ".RGB",
    "Q0 Image File",
    "1.3",
    "An RGB file is a color bitmap image, saved in a file format created by Silicon Graphics (SGI). It contains binary data used to show an image using the RGB color model. RGB files are similar to.SGI files. RGB file open in qView Paul Haeberli invented the RGB format in 1995. It was used primarily to save raster images for display on Silicon Graphics workstations. Both RGB and SGI files contain images comprised of three color channels (red, green, and blue). The similar.RGBA format contains images comprised of three color channels and an alpha channel, which stores transparency information. You can open an RGB file in many image viewers and editors, including File Viewer Plus (Windows), Apple Preview (Mac), XnViewMP (Windows, Mac), and qView (multiplatform). Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. FFmpeg. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. FFmpeg. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. FFmpeg. qViewFree. 24-bit color bitmap image format used by Japanese software; often saved with a.FAL file, which includes header information that describes the RGB image file. Windows XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMPFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. FFmpeg. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. GIMP. ImageMagick. FFmpeg. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. FFmpeg. qView. Windows XnViewMP. Mac XnViewMP.",
    "Most image viewers and editors that can open RGB files can convert them to other image formats. For example, XnViewMP can convert RGB files to the following formats (and many others):.JPEG - JPEG Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.JP2 - JPEG 2000 Core Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image.WEBP - WebP Image."],
